CEO Alex Karp criticized token-based AI pricing, saying enterprises are shifting toward lower-cost models focused on return on investment.

Palantir (NYSE:PLTR) CEO Alex Karp on Wednesday slammed the token-based pricing model used by OpenAI and Anthropic, as rising costs push enterprises toward lower-cost, open-weight models.

“Something has gone completely wrong,” Karp told CNBC’s “Squawk Box,” adding, “I’m not throwing shade at them.”

