cset=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02135909/image-64-1024x618.png 1024w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02135909/image-64-300x181.png 300w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02135909/image-64-768x463.png 768w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02135909/image-64-1536x927.png 1536w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02135909/image-64-2048x1235.png 2048w\\" sizes=\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\" /></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>The Overbought Signal Just Reset</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The sell-off has flushed out an extreme overbought condition.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The 14-day relative strength index has dropped below 50 for the first time since late March, after holding in overbought territory for most of the past two months.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The weekly picture is the same. Weekly RSI has exited overbought after 12 straight weeks above the threshold, the longest such streak of the current cycle.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>That is the kind of reset that tends to interest buyers rather than scare them — at least when the underlying trend is intact.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Not far below current levels lies the 50-day moving average, a technical support level the sector has consistently traded above since early April.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-image size-large\\"><img loading=\\"lazy\\" decoding=\\"async\\" width=\\"1024\\" height=\\"618\\" src=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02140011/image-65-1024x618.png\\" alt=\\"\\" class=\\"wp-image-1535593\\" srcset=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02140011/image-65-1024x618.png 1024w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02140011/image-65-300x181.png 300w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02140011/image-65-768x463.png 768w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02140011/image-65-1536x927.png 1536w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/02140011/image-65-2048x1235.png 2048w\\" sizes=\\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\\" /></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Here&#8217;s The Catch</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Some of the sector&#8217;s favorite names are now the ones analysts rank as the cheapest.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Shares of <strong>Micron Technology Inc.</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MU\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"MU\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MU\\">MU</a>)</a> have fallen roughly 14% this week alone, unwinding part of a near-vertical rally that had made the stock one of the memory supercycle&#8217;s clearest winners.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Yet, Wall Street&#8217;s price targets have not followed the tape lower, indicating the pullback has been driven more by profit taking rather than a change in earnings fundamentals. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Against a price near $963, the median analyst target points to about 60% upside for Micron. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Micron carries the widest implied upside of the three. Against a price near $969, the median analyst target of $1,550 points to about 60% upside.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Cantor Fitzgerald lifted its target to $2,000 from $1,500 on June 29, holding an Overweight rating and setting the Street high. Barclays matched that $2,000 mark on June 25. Raymond James moved to $1,500 from $1,100, reiterating Outperform.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>NVIDIA Corp.</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"NVDA\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\">NVDA</a>)</a> fell 2.5% Thursday to about $193 and screens with roughly 52% upside to the median target. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA/analyst-ratings\\">Benzinga tracks a consensus </a>of $309.13 across 32 analysts.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Broadcom Inc.</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"AVGO\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AVGO\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AVGO\\">AVGO</a>)</a> dropped 2.8% to about $359, leaving roughly 46% upside to the median target. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AVGO/analyst-ratings\\">Benzinga&#8217;s consensus </a>sits at $500.78 across 28 analysts. JP Morgan set the recent high at $580, up from $500, on an Overweight rating, and Jefferies moved to $550.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>TICKER</strong></td><td><strong>LAST PRICE</strong></td><td><strong>MEDIAN PRICE TARGET</strong></td><td><strong>POTENTIAL UPSIDE</strong></td><td><strong>BENZINGA ANALYST RATINGS (MEAN) </strong></td></tr><tr><td>Micron Technology</td><td>$968.56</td><td>$1,550</td><td>+60.03%</td><td>$1,311.43</td></tr><tr><td>Nvidia Corp</td><td>$193.36</td><td>$294</td><td>+52.05%</td><td>$309.13</td></tr><tr><td>Broadcom Inc.</td><td>$358.64</td><td>$525.09</td><td>+46.39%</td><td>$500.78</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\\"wp-element-caption\\"><em>Source: Benzinga Analyst Ratings, Koyfin</em></figcaption></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>What&#8217;s Next?</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The bull case on chipmakers argues that a group up almost 115% in six months is entitled to a two-day flush, and that the RSI reset simply clears the froth.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The bear case is simpler. A trade this crowded priced in perfection, and perfection is a fragile thing.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The question now is whether this is the pause that refreshes the supercycle — or the first crack in the year&#8217;s most crowded trade.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/07/60252913/dow-jones-record-highs-nasdaq-100-sinks-chipmakers-selloff\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nDow Jones Hits Record High as Chip Bloodbath Sinks Nasdaq 100: Stock Market Today</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Photo: Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-07-02T18:58:53Z", "headline": "SOXX ETF''s Worst 2-Day Drop in Over a Year: These 3 Chip Stocks Now Screen with 50% Upside", "id": 60257048, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/07/02/Semiconductors.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/07/02/Semiconductors.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/07/02/Semiconductors.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Semiconductors just posted their sharpest two-day slide since March 2025. The overbought signal that defined the rally has reset.", "symbols": ["AVGO", "MU", "NVDA", "SOXX"], "updated_at": "2026-07-02T18:58:53Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/sector-etfs/26/07/60257048/soxx-etf-selloff-semiconductors-nvidia-micron-broadcom-price-target-upside-potential"}'::jsonb, '03dc136ccf5c1d83bbee1b29db345dc458ab78db66b4fa150ca442ef12565f69', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000060.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/60257048/c074dbacac5a.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:35.874831+00:00'::timestamptz
