Ark sold shares of Advanced Micro Devices across ARKF, ARKQ, ARKX and ARKW. AMD’s stock closed at $506.00, and Ark’s sale of 25,917 shares amounted to approximately $13.1 million.

AMD is currently raising up to $5 billion through a bond sale to boost its AI-related investments. This move is part of AMD’s broader strategy to enhance its AI computing capabilities and manage debt maturities.

## The Palantir Trade

Ark Invest reduced its holdings in Palantir Technologies by selling shares in ARKF. Palantir’s stock closed at $172.55, and the sale of 22,023 shares equated to approximately $3.8 million.

Palantir has taken a unique approach by developing software that integrates with various AI models rather than building its own. This strategy allows Palantir to benefit from the AI boom without heavy investments in AI infrastructure.

