e another 3.75 gigawatts at the site.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>CEO <strong>Jensen Huang </strong>said, &#8220;AI is becoming infrastructure – the foundation for intelligence in every industry – and land, power and shell have become vital in the age of AI.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>He said the project will secure long-term infrastructure for NVIDIA computing systems, allowing OpenAI to expand and continually upgrade its AI capacity as new generations of technology arrive.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>NVIDIA expects the long-lived site to support repeated hardware upgrades. The company estimates that each generation of systems deployed at PORTS-Pike could involve about 1.5 million NVIDIA GPUs and represent roughly <a target=\\"_blank\\" href=\\"https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/securing-the-infrastructure-of-intelligence/\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">$150 billion to $200 billion</a> of NVIDIA revenue.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>NVIDIA will also invest $1.5 billion in SB Energy, joining existing investors<strong> Softbank Group Corp.</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SFTBY\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"SFTBY\\" data-exchange=\\"OTC\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(OTC:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SFTBY\\">SFTBY</a>)</a> and OpenAI.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The investment will support SB Energy’s expansion as an AI infrastructure developer and its commitments to communities surrounding the Ohio project.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">NVIDIA, OpenAI Rework Financing to Reduce Risk</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Separately, NVIDIA and OpenAI are nearing a financing agreement for the Ohio campus that would reduce NVIDIA&#8217;s initial financial guarantee, according to people familiar with the discussions.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The revised structure would cut NVIDIA&#8217;s potential guarantee from $250 billion to less than $120 billion, with NVIDIA initially backing only about half of the planned buildout, the Wall Street Journal <a target=\\"_blank\\" href=\\"https://www.wsj.com/tech/nvidia-downsizes-plans-for-250-billion-guarantee-of-openai-data-center-b56c38d3\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">reported</a> on Friday.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The companies reworked the structure after investors raised concerns about NVIDIA using its balance sheet to support infrastructure spending that ultimately drives demand for its chips.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">OpenAI Commitments Expand NVIDIA&#8217;s Revenue Opportunity</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>OpenAI has committed to substantial NVIDIA infrastructure deployments through 2030, representing about 12 gigawatts of Nvidia computing capacity. That could increase to roughly 16 gigawatts if NVIDIA exercises its option for additional PORTS-Pike capacity.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>At that scale, NVIDIA estimates the OpenAI opportunity could represent about $600 billion of computing systems through 2030.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>NVIDIA argues that frontier AI developers increasingly face computing-capacity constraints because their infrastructure requirements can grow faster than their balance sheets and financing capacity. By helping secure land, power and facilities, NVIDIA aims to remove those constraints while creating long-term demand for successive generations of its AI systems.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Earnings And Analyst Outlook</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The countdown is on: NVIDIA is set to report earnings on August 26, 2026 (confirmed).</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>EPS Estimate</strong>: $2.07 (Up from $1.04 YoY)</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Revenue Estimate</strong>: $91.91 Billion (Up from $46.74 Billion YoY)</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Valuation</strong>: P/E of 34.5x (Indicates premium valuation relative to peers)</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Top ETF Exposure</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>Franklin Focused Dynamic Growth ETF</strong> (NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FFOG\\">FFOG</a>): 9.73% Weight</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>First Trust Innovation Leaders ETF</strong> (NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ILDR\\">ILDR</a>): 9.79% Weight</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Xtrackers Net Zero Pathway Paris Aligned US Equity ETF</strong> (NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/USNZ\\">USNZ</a>): 9.73% Weight</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Significance:</strong> Because NVDA carries such a heavy weight in these funds, any significant inflows or outflows for these ETFs will likely force automatic buying or selling of the stock.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Price Action</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>NVDA Stock Price Activity:</strong> NVIDIA shares were trading higher by 0.40% at $226.04 at the time of publication on Monday, according to <a target=\\"_blank\\" href=\\"https://benzinga.com/services\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">Benzinga Pro data</a>.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Image via Shutterstock</em></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61205810/nvidia-says-free-ai-is-great-for-chips-jensen-huangs-open-source-bet-could-fuel-gpu-demand\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nNVIDIA Says ‘Free AI’ Is Great For Chips — Jensen Huang’s Open-Source Bet Could Fuel GPU Demand</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>", "created_at": "2026-08-17T14:32:31Z", "headline": "NVIDIA’s Ohio AI Megadeal: OpenAI, 8 GW of Compute and a $1.5 Billion SB Energy Bet", "id": 61249540, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/17/Kyiv--Ukraine---January-29--2025-Nvidia-.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/17/Kyiv--Ukraine---January-29--2025-Nvidia-.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/17/Kyiv--Ukraine---January-29--2025-Nvidia-.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "NVIDIA and SB Energy partner to build an 8 IT-GW AI campus in Ohio for OpenAI, backed by a $1.5B investment.", "symbols": ["FFOG", "ILDR", "NVDA", "SFTBY", "USNZ"], "updated_at": "2026-08-17T14:32:31Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61249540/nvidias-ohio-ai-megadeal-openai-8-gw-of-compute-and-a-1-5-billion-sb-energy-bet"}'::jsonb, '5ec6d39dfccd2a1bfb6315119cc4113f2d43a801b45f6dfcf29281218c59f7b5', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000069.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61249540/8be5f2ea87c2.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.022572+00:00'::timestamptz
