rofit (in billions)</strong></th>\\n<th><strong>Revenue Growth</strong></th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>NVIDIA Corp</td>\\n<td>34.46</td>\\n<td>27.88</td>\\n<td>21.71</td>\\n<td>33.06%</td>\\n<td>$71.0</td>\\n<td>$61.16</td>\\n<td>85.23%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Broadcom Inc</td>\\n<td>65.30</td>\\n<td>21.29</td>\\n<td>25.37</td>\\n<td>11.11%</td>\\n<td>$13.07</td>\\n<td>$15.41</td>\\n<td>47.87%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Micron Technology Inc</td>\\n<td>22.87</td>\\n<td>11.34</td>\\n<td>12.77</td>\\n<td>32.62%</td>\\n<td>$35.58</td>\\n<td>$35.06</td>\\n<td>345.72%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Advanced Micro Devices Inc</td>\\n<td>129.08</td>\\n<td>12.29</td>\\n<td>20.21</td>\\n<td>3.49%</td>\\n<td>$3.35</td>\\n<td>$6.2</td>\\n<td>50.11%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Texas Instruments Inc</td>\\n<td>43</td>\\n<td>14.35</td>\\n<td>13.30</td>\\n<td>11.32%</td>\\n<td>$2.95</td>\\n<td>$3.35</td>\\n<td>22.82%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Marvell Technology Inc</td>\\n<td>80.53</td>\\n<td>11.55</td>\\n<td>23.50</td>\\n<td>0.21%</td>\\n<td>$0.66</td>\\n<td>$1.26</td>\\n<td>27.57%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Analog Devices Inc</td>\\n<td>58.08</td>\\n<td>5.63</td>\\n<td>15.10</td>\\n<td>3.48%</td>\\n<td>$1.9</td>\\n<td>$2.44</td>\\n<td>37.25%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Qualcomm Inc</td>\\n<td>18.53</td>\\n<td>6.16</td>\\n<td>3.96</td>\\n<td>7.29%</td>\\n<td>$3.04</td>\\n<td>$5.28</td>\\n<td>-4.03%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Monolithic Power Systems Inc</td>\\n<td>86.39</td>\\n<td>17.86</td>\\n<td>21.17</td>\\n<td>6.8%</td>\\n<td>$0.32</td>\\n<td>$0.54</td>\\n<td>47.56%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>NXP Semiconductors NV</td>\\n<td>46.32</td>\\n<td>5.15</td>\\n<td>24.65</td>\\n<td>6.87%</td>\\n<td>$1.27</td>\\n<td>$2.0</td>\\n<td>19.48%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Credo Technology Group Holding Ltd</td>\\n<td>112.68</td>\\n<td>25.56</td>\\n<td>39.87</td>\\n<td>8.64%</td>\\n<td>$0.17</td>\\n<td>$0.3</td>\\n<td>157.02%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Microchip Technology Inc</td>\\n<td>118.03</td>\\n<td>6.76</td>\\n<td>8.59</td>\\n<td>3.14%</td>\\n<td>$0.49</td>\\n<td>$0.94</td>\\n<td>38.05%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>ON Semiconductor Corp</td>\\n<td>54.50</td>\\n<td>4.50</td>\\n<td>5.43</td>\\n<td>3.12%</td>\\n<td>$0.43</td>\\n<td>$0.62</td>\\n<td>9.18%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Tower Semiconductor Ltd</td>\\n<td>104.24</td>\\n<td>9.66</td>\\n<td>17.61</td>\\n<td>2.99%</td>\\n<td>$0.17</td>\\n<td>$0.14</td>\\n<td>23.66%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>GLOBALFOUNDRIES Inc</td>\\n<td>41.75</td>\\n<td>2.48</td>\\n<td>4.30</td>\\n<td>1.41%</td>\\n<td>$0.48</td>\\n<td>$0.51</td>\\n<td>5.81%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings Inc</td>\\n<td>104.31</td>\\n<td>16.23</td>\\n<td>21.61</td>\\n<td>6.81%</td>\\n<td>$0.14</td>\\n<td>$0.2</td>\\n<td>35.77%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>First Solar Inc</td>\\n<td>22.24</td>\\n<td>2.27</td>\\n<td>23.99</td>\\n<td>4.18%</td>\\n<td>$0.61</td>\\n<td>$0.61</td>\\n<td>-3.73%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><strong>Average</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>69.24</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>10.82</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>17.59</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>7.09%</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>$4.04</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>$4.68</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>53.76%</strong></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\\n\\n<style>\\n        table {\\n            width: 100%;\\n            border-collapse: collapse;\\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\n            font-size: 14px;\\n        }\\n\\n        th, td {\\n            padding: 8px;\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        th {\\n            background-color: #293a5a;\\n            color: #fff;\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        tr:nth-child(even) {\\n            background-color: #f2f4f8;\\n        }\\n\\n        tr:hover {\\n            background-color: #e1e4ea;\\n        }\\n\\n        td:nth-child(3), td:nth-child(5) {\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        .dividend-amount {\\n            font-weight: bold;\\n            color: #0d6efd;\\n        }\\n\\n        .dividend-frequency {\\n            font-size: 12px;\\n            color: #6c757d;\\n        }\\n    </style>\\n\\n<p>Upon a comprehensive analysis of NVIDIA, the following trends can be discerned: </p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<p>The Price to Earnings ratio of <b>34.46</b> is <b>0.5x</b> lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation for the stock.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The elevated Price to Book ratio of <b>27.88</b> relative to the industry average by <b>2.58x</b> suggests company might be overvalued based on its book value.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The Price to Sales ratio of <b>21.71</b>, which is <b>1.23x</b> the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>With a Return on Equity (ROE) of <b>33.06%</b> that is <b>25.97%</b> above the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits efficient use of equity to generate profits.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>With higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of <b>$71.0 Billion</b>, which is <b>17.57x</b> above the industry average, the company demonstrates stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>Compared to its industry, the company has higher gross profit of <b>$61.16 Billion</b>, which indicates <b>13.07x</b> above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The company is experiencing remarkable revenue growth, with a rate of <b>85.23%</b>, outperforming the industry average of <b>53.76%</b>.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Debt To Equity Ratio</h3>\\n<p><img src=\\"https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/18/d84c1bb348593a32867e944f75874142.png\\" alt=\\"debt to equity\\" /></p>\\n\\n<p>The debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio is an important measure to assess the financial structure and risk profile of a company.</p>\\n<p>Considering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.</p>\\n<p>In terms of the Debt-to-Equity ratio, NVIDIA can be assessed by comparing it to its top 4 peers, resulting in the following observations:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<p>Among its top 4 peers, NVIDIA has a stronger financial position with a lower debt-to-equity ratio of <b>0.06</b>.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>This indicates that the company relies less on debt financing and maintains a more favorable balance between debt and equity, which can be viewed positively by investors.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Key Takeaways</h3>\\n<p>For NVIDIA, the PE ratio is low compared to peers, indicating potential undervaluation. The high PB and PS ratios suggest strong market sentiment and revenue multiples. In terms of ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth, NVIDIA outperforms industry peers, reflecting robust financial performance and growth prospects.</p>\\n<p><em>This article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-18T09:58:28Z", "headline": "Understanding NVIDIA''s Position In Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment Industry Compared To Competitors", "id": 61266554, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_9.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_9.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_9.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "In the fast-paced and cutthroat world of business, conducting thorough company analysis is essential for investors and industry experts. In this article, we will undertake a comprehensive industry comparison, evaluating", "symbols": ["NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-18T09:58:28Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/08/61266554/understanding-nvidia-s-position-semiconductors-amp-semiconductor-equipment-industry-compared-competi"}'::jsonb, '9b1a8bfb36cbd625ab707f3aba495bec2f3735431d6659c9cec1d150097cb05e', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000069.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61266554/6c08cf2a46e8.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.097866+00:00'::timestamptz
