ta-ticker=\\"AMZN\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AMZN\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AMZN\\">AMZN</a>)</a> and <strong>Nokia Corp</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"NOK\\" data-exchange=\\"NYSE\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NOK\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NOK\\">NOK</a>)</a> each accounting for more than 10% of annual revenue, underscoring that its growth is increasingly tied to multiple technology leaders rather than a single AI winner.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Fabrinet&#8217;s Customer List Tells a Bigger AI Story</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>One of the most revealing disclosures in Fabrinet&#8217;s fiscal 2026 earnings wasn&#8217;t about revenue or earnings—it was about customer diversification.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>During <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/08/61263037/transcript-fabrinet-q4-2026-earnings-conference-call\\">the earnings call</a>, Chief Financial Officer <strong>Csaba Sverha</strong> said, &#8220;In 2026, we continued to diversify our customer base, with four customers representing 10% or more of total revenue. These were Cisco at 20%, Nvidia at 16%, Nokia at 11%, and Amazon at 11% of total revenue.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>That matters because it suggests Fabrinet&#8217;s AI exposure is becoming broader. Nvidia remains a key customer, but Cisco&#8217;s networking business, Amazon&#8217;s cloud infrastructure and Nokia&#8217;s communications portfolio are also contributing meaningfully to growth. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Rather than relying on one flagship customer, the company appears to be benefiting from spending across multiple parts of the AI and networking ecosystem.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>That&#8217;s management&#8217;s disclosure. The inference is that Fabrinet&#8217;s position in advanced optical manufacturing is becoming more diversified as hyperscalers and networking vendors expand AI infrastructure.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/08/61079756/here-s-how-much-you-would-have-made-owning-fabrinet-stock-last-10-years\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nHere’s How Much You Would Have Made Owning Fabrinet Stock In The Last 10 Years</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">AI Demand Extends Well Beyond One Customer</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Management also struck an unusually confident tone about demand.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>CEO <strong>Seamus Grady</strong> said, &#8220;Demand from these markets continues to increase, which makes us optimistic about the long-term durability of these trends.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Later in the call, he went even further, telling analysts, &#8220;There looks to be, you know, no end in sight to the demand from the customers.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Importantly, management attributed that confidence to multiple growth engines rather than a single product cycle. The company highlighted continued momentum in data center interconnect (DCI), high-performance computing (HPC) and transceivers, while noting that new customer programs are beginning to ramp.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Analysts largely focused their questions on next-generation optical technologies, hyperscaler demand and future capacity, reinforcing that Wall Street is increasingly viewing Fabrinet as a key manufacturing partner for AI networking rather than simply a contract manufacturer.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">What Fabrinet Investors Should Watch Next</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The customer list may be the clearest indication yet that Fabrinet&#8217;s AI opportunity extends beyond any single company. Management has provided evidence of broad demand, diversified customers and expanding production capacity, while analysts continue probing the next wave of AI optical technologies. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>For investors, the key question is no longer whether AI demand is supporting Fabrinet&#8217;s business—it appears to be—but whether the company can continue translating that diversified customer base into sustained growth as new programs move from qualification to volume production.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/08/61266758/fabrinet-ceo-sees-no-end-in-sight-to-data-center-demand\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nFabrinet CEO Sees ‘No End in Sight’ to Data Center Demand</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-18T14:11:42Z", "headline": "Cisco, Nvidia, Amazon and Nokia: The Customer List Behind Fabrinet''s AI Boom (CORRECTED)", "id": 61272428, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/18/Fabrinet.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/18/Fabrinet.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/18/Fabrinet.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Fabrinet&#39;s latest earnings showed Cisco, Nvidia, Amazon and Nokia as its largest customers, highlighting the company&#39;s expanding role in AI infrastructure.", "symbols": ["AMZN", "CSCO", "FN", "NOK", "NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-18T14:11:57Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/08/61272428/cisco-nvidia-amazon-nokia-fabrinet-ai-boom"}'::jsonb, '05665fb4d398c83e497ed83032c10c36bc71a9f575268c11a0d7a03cb2f27e33', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000069.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61272428/7e19ca27307c.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.111575+00:00'::timestamptz
