d>116.43</td>\\n<td>6.66</td>\\n<td>8.47</td>\\n<td>3.14%</td>\\n<td>$0.49</td>\\n<td>$0.94</td>\\n<td>38.05%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>ON Semiconductor Corp</td>\\n<td>54.03</td>\\n<td>4.46</td>\\n<td>5.38</td>\\n<td>3.12%</td>\\n<td>$0.43</td>\\n<td>$0.62</td>\\n<td>9.18%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Tower Semiconductor Ltd</td>\\n<td>104.93</td>\\n<td>9.72</td>\\n<td>17.73</td>\\n<td>2.99%</td>\\n<td>$0.17</td>\\n<td>$0.14</td>\\n<td>23.66%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>GLOBALFOUNDRIES Inc</td>\\n<td>42.64</td>\\n<td>2.53</td>\\n<td>4.39</td>\\n<td>1.41%</td>\\n<td>$0.48</td>\\n<td>$0.51</td>\\n<td>5.81%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>First Solar Inc</td>\\n<td>23.03</td>\\n<td>2.35</td>\\n<td>24.84</td>\\n<td>4.18%</td>\\n<td>$0.61</td>\\n<td>$0.61</td>\\n<td>-3.73%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings Inc</td>\\n<td>100.78</td>\\n<td>15.68</td>\\n<td>20.88</td>\\n<td>6.81%</td>\\n<td>$0.14</td>\\n<td>$0.2</td>\\n<td>35.77%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><strong>Average</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>68.24</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>10.59</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>17.3</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>7.09%</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>$4.04</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>$4.68</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>53.76%</strong></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\\n\\n<style>\\n        table {\\n            width: 100%;\\n            border-collapse: collapse;\\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\n            font-size: 14px;\\n        }\\n\\n        th, td {\\n            padding: 8px;\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        th {\\n            background-color: #293a5a;\\n            color: #fff;\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        tr:nth-child(even) {\\n            background-color: #f2f4f8;\\n        }\\n\\n        tr:hover {\\n            background-color: #e1e4ea;\\n        }\\n\\n        td:nth-child(3), td:nth-child(5) {\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        .dividend-amount {\\n            font-weight: bold;\\n            color: #0d6efd;\\n        }\\n\\n        .dividend-frequency {\\n            font-size: 12px;\\n            color: #6c757d;\\n        }\\n    </style>\\n\\n<p>When closely examining NVIDIA, the following trends emerge: </p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<p>The Price to Earnings ratio of <b>34.48</b> is <b>0.51x</b> lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation for the stock.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>It could be trading at a premium in relation to its book value, as indicated by its Price to Book ratio of <b>27.9</b> which exceeds the industry average by <b>2.63x</b>.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The Price to Sales ratio of <b>21.73</b>, which is <b>1.26x</b> the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>With a Return on Equity (ROE) of <b>33.06%</b> that is <b>25.97%</b> above the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits efficient use of equity to generate profits.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of <b>$71.0 Billion</b> is <b>17.57x</b> above the industry average, highlighting stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>Compared to its industry, the company has higher gross profit of <b>$61.16 Billion</b>, which indicates <b>13.07x</b> above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The company''s revenue growth of <b>85.23%</b> is notably higher compared to the industry average of <b>53.76%</b>, showcasing exceptional sales performance and strong demand for its products or services.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Debt To Equity Ratio</h3>\\n<p><img src=\\"https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/17/d84c1bb348593a32867e944f75874142.png\\" alt=\\"debt to equity\\" /></p>\\n\\n<p>The debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio measures the financial leverage of a company by evaluating its debt relative to its equity.</p>\\n<p>Considering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.</p>\\n<p>When evaluating NVIDIA alongside its top 4 peers in terms of the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following insights arise:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<p>NVIDIA is in a relatively stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers, as evidenced by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of <b>0.06</b>.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>This implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Key Takeaways</h3>\\n<p>For NVIDIA in the Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment industry, the PE, PB, and PS ratios indicate that the stock is relatively undervalued compared to its peers. On the other hand, the high ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth suggest that NVIDIA is performing exceptionally well in terms of profitability and operational efficiency within the industry sector.</p>\\n<p><em>This article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-17T09:58:23Z", "headline": "Understanding NVIDIA''s Position In Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment Industry Compared To Competitors", "id": 61240146, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_2.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_2.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_2.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "In today&#39;s fast-paced and competitive business landscape, it is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts to thoroughly analyze companies before making investment decisions. In this article, we will conduct a", "symbols": ["NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-17T09:58:23Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/08/61240146/understanding-nvidia-s-position-semiconductors-amp-semiconductor-equipment-industry-compared-competi"}'::jsonb, 'a7b2c89fec1ef1eca65a1d634ee6c5da1bf69ba236878e162d624a1518aa10b1', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000069.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61240146/360fba927eeb.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:35.967081+00:00'::timestamptz
