\"noopener\\">\\nMark Zuckerberg’s Meta Agreed to a $17 Billion Settlement—Bernie Sanders Calls It a ‘Good Step Forward,’ But Says &#039;Much More Needs to Be Done&#039;</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p>Nvidia guided third-quarter revenue to between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion and ended the quarter with $99.0 billion remaining under its share repurchase authorization.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Proposed Tariff Discussions</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Separately, eight people familiar with discussions <a target=\\"_blank\\" href=\\"https://www.politico.com/news/2026/08/27/data-centers-chips-tariffs-threat-01050957\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">told</a> POLITICO that the <strong>Trump</strong> administration is weighing a new round of sweeping tariffs on semiconductors.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>One tariff approach under consideration would expand the tech products subject to duties, hitting chips as well as laptops, gaming consoles, and data center servers, the people said.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Four of the people noted Commerce Secretary <strong>Howard Lutnick </strong>favors a structure tying foreign companies’ tariff relief to U.S. chip manufacturing investments to boost domestic production.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Technical Analysis</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Even with today’s bounce, Intel is still in a shorter-term downtrend: the stock is trading 7.3% below its 20-day SMA ($95.73) and 15.9% below its 50-day SMA ($105.48), which keeps overhead supply in focus on rallies. At the same time, it remains 22.3% above its 200-day SMA ($72.51), so the longer-term trend still looks constructive despite the mid-year drawdown.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The 20-day SMA sitting below the 50-day SMA is a bearish crossover that often shows the market is still \\"working off\\" a prior run, and it fits with the break below support that showed up in July.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The June swing high (which also marked the 52-week high at $142.35) and the July swing low frame the current range traders are watching, with price trying to stabilize in the middle of that reset.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>INTC Stock Price Activity:</strong> Intel shares were up 3.30% at $91.95 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to <a target=\\"_blank\\" href=\\"https://benzinga.com/services\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">Benzinga Pro data</a>.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61459773/jim-cramer-has-a-message-for-nvidia-investors-after-the-earnings-blowout-dont-let-the-bears-deceive-you-into-selling-nvda\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nJim Cramer Has a Message for Nvidia Investors After the Earnings Blowout: ‘Don’t Let the Bears Deceive You’ Into Selling NVDA</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Image via Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-27T14:58:18Z", "headline": "Why Is Intel Stock Surging on Thursday?", "id": 61467962, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/New-York-City--New-York---September-18-2.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/New-York-City--New-York---September-18-2.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/New-York-City--New-York---September-18-2.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Intel Corp. (INTC) stock is surging Thursday following Nvidia’s strong Q2 financial results and reports of potential broad U.S. chip tariffs.", "symbols": ["INTC", "NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-27T14:58:18Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/08/61467962/why-is-intel-stock-surging-on-thursday"}'::jsonb, 'ee74e6d48b84d30f3bd20e5a235b05585a98a068eaa30ac71d1e5a9f1fa0372e', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61467962/77f9eba5cf28.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.829580+00:00'::timestamptz
