- S&P 500 slipped 0.1% to 7,668.85, shedding roughly 8 points.
- Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 0.2% to 53,446.13, giving back about 123 points.
- Russell 2000 fell 0.3% to 3,000.42, clinging to the 3,000 handle.
- Gold sank 1.3% to $4,599.33 an ounce as in-line core inflation and firmer yields sapped bullion demand, dragging the SPDR Gold Shares (NYSE:GLD) lower.
- Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) eased 0.7% to $78,000.

The yield on the 10-year Treasury note rose 4 basis points to 4.67% as the inflation data undercut the case for easing. The 2-year yield added 4 basis points to 4.23%, while the 30-year held at 5.19%.

