INSERT INTO document_revision_source (revision_id, raw_payload, raw_payload_sha256, raw_document, raw_document_sha256, raw_document_url, raw_file_refs, stored_at)
SELECT (SELECT r.revision_id FROM document_revision r JOIN document d ON d.document_id = r.document_id WHERE d.provider_id = (SELECT provider_id FROM provider WHERE code = 'alpaca') AND d.source_namespace = 'news' AND d.source_record_id = '61441583' AND NOT d.is_sample AND r.source_snapshot_hash = '9491f7a1e4268875071a7a2c5be074a88a1a194401f58f41a1ccf7c8c43d38b6' AND r.preprocessing_version = 'ingest-1'),  E'{"author": "Piero Cingari", "content": "<p>U.S. equities drifted in a narrow band by midday Wednesday as investors refused to commit capital ahead of <strong>Nvidia Corp. </strong><a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"NVDA\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\">NVDA</a>)</a>&#8216;s after-the-bell results, while a hotter-than-forecast July inflation print revived talk <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/economic-data/26/08/61431642/pce-report-july-personal-consumption-expenditure-fed-favorite-inflation\\">of a September rate hike.</a></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The Personal Consumption Expenditures (PCE) price index rose 0.2% month-over-month in July, matching forecasts of 0.1%, while the annual rate held at 3.7% versus expectations of 3.6%. Core PCE held at 3.3% year-over-year, still well north of the Federal Reserve&#8217;s 2% target.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Second-quarter GDP growth was confirmed at an annualized 1.5%, down from 2.1% in the first quarter. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li>Nasdaq 100, the weakest major benchmark, dropped 0.6% to 29,041.12 for a 168-point decline. </li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>S&amp;P 500 slipped 0.1% to 7,668.85, shedding roughly 8 points. </li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 0.2% to 53,446.13, giving back about 123 points.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Russell 2000 fell 0.3% to 3,000.42, clinging to the 3,000 handle.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Gold sank 1.3% to $4,599.33 an ounce as in-line core inflation and firmer yields sapped bullion demand, dragging the <strong>SPDR Gold Shares <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GLD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GLD\\">GLD</a>)</a></strong> lower. </li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Bitcoin</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"BTC\\" data-exchange=\\"CRYPTO\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BTC-USD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(CRYPTO: BTC)</a> eased 0.7% to $78,000.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The yield on the 10-year Treasury note rose 4 basis points to 4.67% as the inflation data undercut the case for easing. The 2-year yield added 4 basis points to 4.23%, while the 30-year held at 5.19%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Traders now look to Fed Chair <strong>Kevin Warsh</strong>&#8216;s <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/topic/jackson-hole\\">Jackson Hole</a> address on Friday for direction ahead of the Sept. 16 policy meeting, with markets increasingly unwilling to rule out a hike.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Wednesday&#8217;s Performance In Major US Indices</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><thead><tr><th>Index</th><th>Last</th><th>% Change</th><th>MTD</th><th>YTD</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>S&amp;P 500</td><td>7,665.85</td><td>-0.1%</td><td>+2.4%</td><td>+12.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Dow Jones</td><td>53,420.85</td><td>-0.3%</td><td>+1.8%</td><td>+11.1%</td></tr><tr><td>Nasdaq 100</td><td>29,041.12</td><td>-0.6%</td><td>+2.7%</td><td>+15.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Russell 2000</td><td>3,000.42</td><td>-0.3%</td><td>+2.4%</td><td>+20.9%</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\\"wp-element-caption\\"><em>Updated by 12:30 PM ET</em></figcaption></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>According to the&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://bzresearch.myclickfunnels.com/benzinga-pro-content-webinar-registration/?utm_source=BZprocontent082626&amp;t=be2bearmibe3na1\\">Benzinga Pro</a>&nbsp;platform:</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>Vanguard S&amp;P 500 ETF&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/VOO\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/VOO\\">VOO</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;slipped 0.1%.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DIA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DIA\\">DIA</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;fell 0.3%.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>Invesco QQQ Trust&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/QQQ\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/QQQ\\">QQQ</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;declined 0.6%.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>iShares Russell 2000 ETF&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IWM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IWM\\">IWM</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;eased 0.3%.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Energy Stocks Rise, Tech Holds Steady Ahead of Nvidia&#8217;s Results</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Energy Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLE\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLE\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLE\\">XLE</a>)</a> led all 11 S&amp;P 500 sectors with a 1.5% gain as crude reversed higher, extending its year-to-date advance to 42.7%. The&nbsp;<strong>Industrials Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLI\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLI\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLI\\">XLI</a>)</a> followed at 1.1%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>At the other end, the&nbsp;<strong>Consumer Discretionary Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLY\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLY\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLY\\">XLY</a>)</a> and the&nbsp;<strong>Health Care Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLV\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLV\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLV\\">XLV</a>)</a> each fell 1.0%. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLK\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLK\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLK\\">XLK</a>)</a> held a 0.2% gain despite the Nvidia-related caution in the index.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Precious-metals equities took the worst of it, as the&nbsp;<strong>VanEck Gold Miners ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GDX\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"GDX\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GDX\\">GDX</a>)</a> tumbled 2.7% alongside bullion and&nbsp;<strong>AngloGold Ashanti plc&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AU\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AU\\">AU</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;dropped 4.3%. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Invesco WilderHill Clean Energy ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/PBW\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"PBW\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/PBW\\">PBW</a>)</a> shed 1.5%, while the&nbsp;<strong>SPDR S&amp;P Insurance ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/KIE\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"KIE\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/KIE\\">KIE</a>)</a> rose 0.5% and the&nbsp;<strong>VanEck Agribusiness ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MOO\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"MOO\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MOO\\">MOO</a>)</a> added 0.4%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Pipeline Operators — The Day&#8217;s Cleanest Trade </h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>DT Midstream Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DTM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DTM\\">DTM</a>)</a></strong> rose 5.1%, <strong>The Williams Companies Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/WMB\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/WMB\\">WMB</a>)</a></strong> gained 4.6% and <strong>Kinder Morgan Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/KMI\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/KMI\\">KMI</a>)</a></strong> added 4.1% as natural gas jumped. <strong>C.H. Robinson Worldwide Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CHRW\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CHRW\\">CHRW</a>)</a></strong> climbed 5.3% and <strong>The J. M. Smucker Company <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SJM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SJM\\">SJM</a>)</a></strong> rose 4.0%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Semtech Corp.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMTC\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMTC\\">SMTC</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;led the Russell 1000 with an 8.1% surge after reporting record fiscal second-quarter net sales of $341.9 million late Tuesday, up 33% year-over-year, with data center revenue hitting a record $100 million on 800G and 1.6T demand. Semtech guided next-quarter revenue to roughly $410 million at the midpoint, about 15% above consensus.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>TTM Technologies Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TTMI\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TTMI\\">TTMI</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;rose 6.6%, trading in sympathy with the AI-hardware complex ahead of Nvidia&#8217;s print. Peers moved with it, as&nbsp;<strong>Arista Networks Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ANET\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ANET\\">ANET</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;gained 3.9% and&nbsp;<strong>Lumentum Holdings Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/LITE\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/LITE\\">LITE</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;added 3.8%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Summit Therapeutics Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMMT\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMMT\\">SMMT</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;climbed 6.6%. The move follows a roughly 25% one-month drawdown and comes ahead of the FDA&#8217;s decision on ivonescimab expected by mid-November.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Retail Delivers Session&#8217;s Other Upside </h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Bath &amp; Body Works Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BBWI\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BBWI\\">BBWI</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;jumped 6.4% after posting adjusted earnings of 62 cents per share against a 25-cent consensus and lifting full-year adjusted EPS guidance to $2.60-$2.80 from $2.40-$2.65, marking its first direct net sales growth since 2021 – enough to override a third-quarter forecast of 7 to 12 cents versus 26 cents expected.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>The Gap Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GAP\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GAP\\">GAP</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;rallied 5.7%, riding the read-across into its own second-quarter report due Thursday after the close.&nbsp;<strong>DICK&#8217;S Sporting Goods Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DKS\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DKS\\">DKS</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;tacked on 3.2%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The day&#8217;s most brutal reaction? <strong>Dycom Industries Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DY\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DY\\">DY</a>)</a></strong>. The provider of specialty contracting services&#8217; stock price dipped 11.3% despite record fiscal second-quarter contract revenue of about $2 billion, up 45.6%, adjusted EPS of $5.29, backlog of $12.24 billion, up 53.2%, and a raised full-year outlook.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Zoom Communications Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ZM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ZM\\">ZM</a>)</a></strong> tumbled 7.8% even after beating with adjusted EPS of $1.55 against $1.48 expected and raising full-year fiscal 2027 revenue, EPS, and free cash flow guidance. Total revenue growth of just 4.9% left investors underwhelmed on the pace of AI monetization.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Moderna Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MRNA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MRNA\\">MRNA</a>)</a></strong> dropped 7.4% as profit-taking extended into a fourth session following last week&#8217;s 177% single-day surge on late-stage melanoma data for its personalized cancer vaccine. <strong>Caris Life Sciences Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CAI\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CAI\\">CAI</a>)</a></strong> fell 5.9% with no confirmed catalyst on the tape, last reporting on Aug. 5.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Elsewhere,&nbsp;<strong>Intuit Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/INTU\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/INTU\\">INTU</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;slid 4.5% after guiding fiscal 2027 revenue to $23.28 billion-$23.51 billion, implying 9% to 10% growth, with Mailchimp seen flat to down 1%.&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Boston Scientific Corp. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BSX\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BSX\\">BSX</a>)</a></strong> lost 4.6%, and <strong>Eli Lilly and Co. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/LLY\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/LLY\\">LLY</a>)</a></strong> fell 3.5%, weighing on healthcare.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Crypto-linked equities also came under pressure, with Bitcoin down 0.8% near $78,000. <strong>Coinbase Global Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/COIN\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/COIN\\">COIN</a>)</a></strong> fell 3.8%, <strong>Strategy Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSTR\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSTR\\">MSTR</a>)</a></strong> lost 3.7%, and <strong>IREN Ltd. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IREN\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IREN\\">IREN</a>)</a></strong> dropped 5.5%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Wednesday&#8217;s Russell 1000 Top Gainers</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>% change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Semtech Corporation</strong></td><td>+8.11%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>TTM Technologies, Inc.</strong></td><td>+6.62%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Summit Therapeutics Inc.</strong></td><td>+6.59%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Bath &amp; Body Works, Inc.</strong></td><td>+6.42%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>The Gap, Inc.</strong></td><td>+5.65%</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Wednesday&#8217;s Russell 1000 Top Losers</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>% change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Dycom Industries, Inc.</strong></td><td>-11.28%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Figure Technology Solutions, Inc.</strong> <strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FIGR\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FIGR\\">FIGR</a>)</a></strong></td><td>-9.56%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Zoom Communications, Inc.</strong></td><td>-7.75%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Moderna, Inc.</strong></td><td>-7.41%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Caris Life Sciences, Inc.</strong></td><td>-5.92%</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Image: Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-26T16:58:34Z", "headline": "Nasdaq 100 Falls as Hot PCE Inflation Stirs Rate-Hike Bets: Stock Market Today", "id": 61441583, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Stocks-Fall--Technology-Businesses-Do-No.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Stocks-Fall--Technology-Businesses-Do-No.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Stocks-Fall--Technology-Businesses-Do-No.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Nasdaq 100 falls 0.6% as traders wait on Nvidia and hot July PCE revives September rate-hike bets. Energy leads, gold sinks 1.3% to $4,599.", "symbols": ["ANET", "AU", "BBWI", "BSX", "BTCUSD", "CAI", "CHRW", "COIN", "DIA", "DKS", "DTM", "DY", "FIGR", "GAP", "GDX", "GLD", "INTU", "IREN", "IWM", "KIE", "KMI", "LITE", "LLY", "MOO", "MRNA", "MSTR", "NVDA", "PBW", "QQQ", "SJM", "SMMT", "SMTC", "TTMI", "VOO", "WMB", "XLE", "XLI", "XLK", "XLV", "XLY", "ZM"], "updated_at": "2026-08-26T16:58:34Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61441583/stock-market-today-nvidia-jitters-drag-nasdaq-hot-pce-rate-hike-bets"}'::jsonb, '87b1962380121c871bedea5163998fc3deb985f71fc5b511a12d58a150715758', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61441583/9491f7a1e426.j