Inc. </strong><a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"AVGO\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AVGO\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/AVGO\\">AVGO</a>)</a> climbed 4.44%, 2.82%, 1.73%, and 1.85%, respectively. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Nvidia&#8217;s CFO,&nbsp;<strong>Colette Kress</strong>, stated on Wednesday that the company&nbsp;projected a&nbsp;revenue growth of 70% for&nbsp;fiscal 2028, spanning&nbsp;from February 2027 to January&nbsp;2028.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>CEO&nbsp;<strong>Jensen Huang</strong>&nbsp;mentioned that the demand is &#8220;much greater than 70%,&#8221; but the company&#8217;s capacity to supply products is presently restricted. Nvidia&#8217;s key manufacturer, <strong>Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co Ltd.</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"TSM\\" data-exchange=\\"NYSE\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TSM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TSM\\">TSM</a>)</a>, is still dealing with supply constraints, and memory chips, a vital part of Nvidia&#8217;s systems, continue to be in short supply.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Huang added that Nvidia has &#8220;never forecasted&#8221;&nbsp;a year in advance, but&nbsp;now the company has &#8220;a lot greater visibility&#8221; across the supply chain, allowing it to do so.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61453544/nvidia-jensen-huang-openai-jalapeno-chip-competition\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang Not Taking OpenAI&#039;s &#039;Jalapeño&#039; Chip Personally: &#039;Lots of Projects Get Started. Lots of Projects Get Canceled&#039;</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Nvidia Doubles Down on AI Expansion</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The company&#8217;s witnessed a 106% year-over-year increase in revenue in the second quarter, reaching $96.22 billion. Huang said that the &#8220;AI infrastructure buildout is at full steam,&#8221; indicating Nvidia’s aggressive expansion in the AI sector. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Nvidia could see its <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/earnings/26/08/61452739/nvidia-revenue-18x-growth-4-years-analyst-history\\">revenue surge</a> roughly 1,730% in four years if it meets its $108 billion third quarter guidance, a growth rate <strong>The Kobeissi Letter</strong> called unmatched in modern corporate history for a company of its size.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Meanwhile, the chipmaker has also reportedly <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61453368/nvidia-agrees-to-acquire-hugging-face-for-12-9-billion-in-one-of-its-largest-acquisitions-so-far-as-it-expands-control-of-open-source-ai-models-report\\">agreed to acquire </a><strong>Hugging Face</strong>, an open-source AI model repository, for a whopping $12.9 billion, adding to the company&#8217;s control over open-source AI models. This acquisition is one of Nvidia&#8217;s largest to date, second only to the $20 billion <strong>Groq </strong>acquisition.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Disclaimer</em>:</strong><em>&nbsp;This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors</em>.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61399459/jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-childhood-wasnt-good-kid\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nJensen Huang Once Revealed He &#039;Wasn&#039;t A Particularly Good Kid&#039; but One That &#039;Just Turned Out Good&#039; — Here&#039;s Something Today&#039;s Nvidia CEO Knew Even at a Young Age</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Photo courtesy: Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-27T09:31:57Z", "headline": "Nvidia Stock Climbs Over 7% in Thursday Pre-Market: What’s Lifting Micron, Intel and Other Chip Stocks?", "id": 61454195, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Los-Angeles--California---July-6-2025-Nv.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Los-Angeles--California---July-6-2025-Nv.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Los-Angeles--California---July-6-2025-Nv.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Nvidia shares surge 7.4% premarket as strong guidance boosts chip stocks, while CEO Jensen Huang cites robust AI demand.", "symbols": ["AMD", "AVGO", "INTC", "MU", "NVDA", "TSM"], "updated_at": "2026-08-27T09:32:06Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61454195/nvidia-micron-intel-climb-in-thursday-pre-market-whats-going-on"}'::jsonb, '16934231b88dbe478ba3acfd59079c4fe439e278790e0b36f7dbc022f8c3402d', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61454195/6251984584f1.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.600046+00:00'::timestamptz
