 filing formally disclosed Nvidia’s agreement with <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61236075/nvidia-3-billion-investment-sb-energy-openai-data-center\\">SoftBank’s SB Energy</a> for an OpenAI-leased data center. According to the 10-Q, Nvidia has entered into guarantees, &#8220;capped at a total of $105 billion,&#8221; to provide credit support for a land, power, and shell buildout on behalf of OpenAI at SB Energy&#8217;s PORTS Technology Campus in Ohio.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The filing notes that the <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61374193/nvidia-poolside-6-billion-openai-deepseek-ai-model\\">campus involves leases</a> for &#8220;approximately 4.25 gigawatts of IT load&#8221; and will &#8220;exclusively host NVIDIA AI infrastructure.&#8221; Pointing to these massive commitments as evidence of a self-reinforcing financial loop, Burry offered a stark four-word warning: &#8220;Whistling past the graveyard.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x\\"><div class=\\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\\">\\n<blockquote class=\\"twitter-tweet\\" data-width=\\"500\\" data-dnt=\\"true\\"><p lang=\\"en\\" dir=\\"ltr\\">Whistling past the graveyard <a href=\\"https://t.co/KyjxLemeId\\">https://t.co/KyjxLemeId</a></p>&mdash; Cassandra Unchained (@michaeljburry) <a href=\\"https://x.com/michaeljburry/status/2093114771428303237?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\\">August 27, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src=\\"https://platform.x.com/widgets.js\\" charset=\\"utf-8\\"></script>\\n</div></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61454001/michael-burry-says-nvda-stock-appears-wildly-undervalued-on-paper-after-blowout-q2-earnings-but-warns-nvidia-shares-are-still-treading-water\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nMichael Burry Says NVDA Stock Appears ‘Wildly Undervalued’ on Paper After Blowout Q2 Earnings, but Warns Nvidia Shares Are Still ‘Treading Water’</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>NVDA Management Downplays Circular Financing Concerns</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Burry’s attack directly challenges Nvidia management, who aggressively defended their balance sheet strategy during their latest earnings call. Addressing the massive OpenAI guarantees, executives pushed back against critics alleging the company is simply funding its own demand.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>CFO <strong>Colette Kress</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/earnings/26/08/61457781/nvda-downplays-circular-financing-concerns-days-after-michael-burry-called-it-a-wall-street-stunt-we-see-it-differently\\">directly tackled the controversy</a> during her prepared remarks. &#8220;We recognize the scale of this support, and we know some will call this circular financing. We see it differently.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Huang was equally resolute in dismissing the idea that these private credit deals artificially inflate revenue. Defending the Ohio project, Huang stated, &#8220;No. OpenAI will pay the lease.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>The Bear vs. The Bull</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>While Huang frames the massive capital deployment as a necessary masterstroke to secure infrastructure for frontier AI labs that are outgrowing their credit profiles, Burry remains deeply skeptical.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Even after buying December Nvidia call options as a hedge against his bearish position, Burry maintains <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61135655/michael-burry-calls-nvidias-500-billion-ai-financing-push-a-wall-street-stunt-meet-the-new-boss\\">a massive short position</a> against the broader AI ecosystem, insisting that the mechanics revealed in the 10-Q validate his long-term bearish thesis.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>How Has Nvidia Performed in 2026?</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>At the last check, the NVDA stock was trading 0.64% lower in overnight trading. It was up 22.24% year-to-date, advanced by 25.54% over the last year, and rose 28.66% over the last six months. It closed 8.74% higher at $227.98 per share on Thursday.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings</strong> indicate that NVDA maintains a strong price trend in the short, long, and medium terms, with a solid growth score.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\\"><a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\"><img loading=\\"lazy\\" decoding=\\"async\\" width=\\"767\\" height=\\"111\\" src=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/28023943/NVDA-EDGE-AUG-28.png\\" alt=\\"Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings for NVDA.\\" class=\\"wp-image-1622045\\" style=\\"width:920px;height:auto\\" srcset=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/28023943/NVDA-EDGE-AUG-28.png 767w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/28023943/NVDA-EDGE-AUG-28-300x43.png 300w\\" sizes=\\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 767px\\" /></a></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/earnings/26/08/61457781/nvda-downplays-circular-financing-concerns-days-after-michael-burry-called-it-a-wall-street-stunt-we-see-it-differently\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nNVDA Downplays &#039;Circular Financing&#039; Concerns Days After Michael Burry Called it a Wall Street Stunt: &#039;We See it Differently&#039;</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><strong><em>Disclaimer:</em></strong><em> This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-28T07:44:07Z", "headline": "Michael Burry Points to Nvidia''s $105B OpenAI Guarantee as ''Circular Financing'' Red Flag: ''Whistling Past the Graveyard''", "id": 61486426, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/28/Paris--France---January-23--2026-The-Nvi.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/28/Paris--France---January-23--2026-The-Nvi.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/28/Paris--France---January-23--2026-The-Nvi.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Michael Burry calls market reaction &#39;whistling past the graveyard,&#39; citing Nvidia&#39;s 10-Q as proof of a $105B circular financing scheme.", "symbols": ["NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-28T07:44:07Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/earnings/26/08/61486426/michael-burry-points-to-nvidias-105b-openai-guarantee-as-circular-financing-red-flag-whistling-past-the-graveyard"}'::jsonb, '3229ccf2853039e190990d071a6f798f445f5f283fcfab35aa53c5a7186e3579', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61486426/53f4923dd664.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.971075+00:00'::timestamptz
