\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61454001/michael-burry-says-nvda-stock-appears-wildly-undervalued-on-paper-after-blowout-q2-earnings-but-warns-nvidia-shares-are-still-treading-water\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nMichael Burry Says NVDA Stock Appears ‘Wildly Undervalued’ on Paper After Blowout Q2 Earnings, but Warns Nvidia Shares Are Still ‘Treading Water’</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Cues From Last Session</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Health care, communication services, and consumer discretionary stocks recorded the biggest losses on Wednesday as most S&amp;P 500 sectors closed lower, though industrials and utilities bucked the market trend to finish higher.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Index</strong></td><td><strong>Performance (+/-)</strong></td><td><strong>Value</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Dow Jones</td><td>-0.21%</td><td>53,463.88</td></tr><tr><td>S&amp;P 500</td><td>-0.021%</td><td>7,675.70</td></tr><tr><td>Nasdaq Composite</td><td>-0.081%</td><td>26,130.20</td></tr><tr><td>Russell 2000</td><td>-0.14%</td><td>3,005.90</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Insights From Analysts</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>BlackRock </strong>foresees an unconventional landscape for the U.S. stock market and broader economy, driven by structural shifts rather than a typical business cycle. Despite rising long-term government bond yields, corporate profit forecasts continue to climb.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The BlackRock Investment Institute notes that these dual signals reflect a &#8220;structurally higher cost of capital&#8221; that calls for a fresh approach to portfolio design.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Rather than anticipating a classic downturn, BlackRock remains overweight on U.S. equities. They project U.S. corporate earnings to expand by 11.6% annually over the next five years—a growth trajectory matched in &#8220;only about 15% of historical five-year periods.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>This optimistic outlook relies heavily on technological adoption. As BlackRock highlights, this projection is &#8220;conditional on AI adoption boosting productivity and profit margins.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Economically, intense capital competition among governments and tech hyperscalers is keeping upward pressure on long-term yields. BlackRock emphasizes that &#8220;long-standing macro anchors investors have come to rely upon, such as stable inflation expectations, become less reliable,&#8221; requiring investors to focus on underlying risk drivers over simple asset labels.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Upcoming Economic Data</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Here’s what investors will be keeping an eye on Thursday.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>Initial Jobless Claims:</strong> Decreased by 4,000 to 203,000 for the week ending Aug. 22; the 4-week moving average rose slightly by 1,250 to 205,500.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Goods Trade Deficit:</strong> Widened 17.2% month-over-month to $118.8 billion in July, driven by a 2.9% drop in exports ($199.4 billion) and a 3.7% jump in imports ($318.2 billion).</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Wholesale Inventories:</strong> Increased 1.3% month-over-month to $959.1 billion in July, up 5.7% from July 2025.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li><strong>Retail Inventories:</strong> Rose 0.7% month-over-month to $838.5 billion in July, marking a 3.8% increase year-over-year.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>August&#8217;s Kansas City Fed survey data will be released by 11:00 a.m. ET.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Commodities, Crypto, And Global Equity Markets</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Crude Oil WTI futures were trading lower in the early New York session by 0.73% to hover around $81.63 per barrel.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Gold Spot US Dollar fell 0.11% to hover around $4,599.73 per ounce. The U.S. Dollar Index spot was 0.01% higher at the 99.1680 level.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Meanwhile, <strong>Bitcoin </strong><a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"BTC\\" data-exchange=\\"CRYPTO\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BTC-USD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(CRYPTO: BTC)</a> was trading 1.30% higher at $79,836.71 per coin over the last 24 hours.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Asian markets were mixed on Thursday, as South Korea’s Kospi and China&#8217;s CSI 300 indices rose. Australia’s ASX 200, India&#8217;s Nifty 50, Hong Kong’s Hang Seng, and Japan’s Nikkei 225 indices fell. European markets were mostly lower in early trading.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/08/61453735/salesforce-ceo-dismisses-saaspocalypse-fears-as-nonsense-after-crms-record-q2-time-for-it-to-stop\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nSalesforce CEO Dismisses ‘SaaSpocalypse’ Fears as ‘Nonsense’ After CRM’s Record Q2: ‘Time for It to Stop’</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Photo courtesy: Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-27T12:59:57Z", "headline": "Stock Market Today: S&P 500, Nasdaq 100 Futures Gain Following NVDA Blockbuster Q2 Report— CRM, CRWD, HPQ in Focus (UPDATED)", "id": 61454942, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Close-Up-Of-Wall-Street-Sign-With-Iconic.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Close-Up-Of-Wall-Street-Sign-With-Iconic.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Close-Up-Of-Wall-Street-Sign-With-Iconic.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "U.S. stock futures were higher on Thursday, as the Dow Jones index slipped, while the S&amp;P 500, and Nasdaq 100 indices rose.", "symbols": ["BTCUSD", "CRM", "CRWD", "HPQ", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SPY", "ULTA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-27T13:00:11Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61454942/stock-market-today-sp-500-nasdaq-100-futures-gain-while-dow-slips-following-nvda-blockbuster-q2-report-crm-crwd-hpq-in-focus"}'::jsonb, 'fd7de8e2a18edfe8c25208c647b9632a65f0073f012b5ed0cf329ad20fc539c1', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61454942/e8d78d311b0c.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.637955+00:00'::timestamptz
