SELECT d.document_id, (SELECT publisher_id FROM publisher WHERE canonical_key = 'benzinga'), 'media_report', 'Nvidia, Best Buy and 3 Stocks to Watch Heading Into Thursday', false, 'Avi Kapoor', 'U.S. stock futures trade higher, focusing on Best Buy, NVIDIA, Dollar General, HP, and Ulta Beauty for earnings results today.', 'With U.S. stock futures trading higher this morning on Thursday, some of the stocks that may grab investor focus today are as follows:

- Wall Street expects Best Buy Co. Inc. (NYSE:BBY) to post quarterly earnings of $1.38 per share on revenue of $9.59 billion before the opening bell, according to Benzinga Pro data. Best Buy shares rose 1% to $88.34 in after-hours trading.
- Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) reported better-than-expected second-quarter financial results and issued a strong revenue forecast for the current quarter. Nvidia reported second-quarter revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year-over-year. The revenue total beat a Street consensus estimate of $92.18 billion, according to data from Benzinga Pro. Nvidia shares gained 4.7% to $219.53 in the after-hours trading session.
- Analysts are expecting Dollar General Corp. (NYSE:DG) to post quarterly earnings of $2.00 per share on revenue of $11.19 billion before the opening bell. Dollar General shares rose 1.1% to $124.16 in the after-hours trading session.

Check out our premarket coverage here

- HP Inc. (NYSE:HPQ) posted upbeat results for the third quarter and raised its FY2026 earnings forecast. HP reported quarterly earnings of 83 cents per share, which beat the analyst estimate of 69 cents. Quarterly revenue came in at $15.68 billion, which beat the Street estimate of $14.43 billion and was up from $13.93 billion in the same period last year. HP shares dipped 9% to $27.77 in the after-hours trading session.
- Analysts expect Ulta Beauty Inc. (NASDAQ:ULTA) to post quarterly earnings of $6.18 per share on revenue of $2.95 billion after the closing bell. Ulta Beauty shares rose 0.3% to $545.00 in after-hours trading.

Photo courtesy: Prashanth Bala / Shutterstock.com', 'Nvidia, Best Buy and 3 Stocks to Watch Heading Into Thursday

U.S. stock futures trade higher, focusing on Best Buy, NVIDIA, Dollar General, HP, and Ulta Beauty for earnings results today.

With U.S. stock futures trading higher this morning on Thursday, some of the stocks that may grab investor focus today are as follows:

- Wall Street expects Best Buy Co. Inc. (NYSE:BBY) to post quarterly earnings of $1.38 per share on revenue of $9.59 billion before the opening bell, according to Benzinga Pro data. Best Buy shares rose 1% to $88.34 in after-hours trading.
- Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) reported better-than-expected second-quarter financial results and issued a strong revenue forecast for the current quarter. Nvidia reported second-quarter revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year-over-year. The revenue total beat a Street consensus estimate of $92.18 billion, according to data from Benzinga Pro. Nvidia shares gained 4.7% to $219.53 in the after-hours trading session.
- Analysts are expecting Dollar General Corp. (NYSE:DG) to post quarterly earnings of $2.00 per share on revenue of $11.19 billion before the opening bell. Dollar General shares rose 1.1% to $124.16 in the after-hours trading session.

Check out our premarket coverage here

- HP Inc. (NYSE:HPQ) posted upbeat results for the third quarter and raised its FY2026 earnings forecast. HP reported quarterly earnings of 83 cents per share, which beat the analyst estimate of 69 cents. Quarterly revenue came in at $15.68 billion, which beat the Street estimate of $14.43 billion and was up from $13.93 billion in the same period last year. HP shares dipped 9% to $27.77 in the after-hours trading session.
- Analysts expect Ulta Beauty Inc. (NASDAQ:ULTA) to post quarterly earnings of $6.18 per share on revenue of $2.95 billion after the closing bell. Ulta Beauty shares rose 0.3% to $545.00 in after-hours trading.

