SELECT (SELECT r.revision_id FROM document_revision r JOIN document d ON d.document_id = r.document_id WHERE d.provider_id = (SELECT provider_id FROM provider WHERE code = 'alpaca') AND d.source_namespace = 'news' AND d.source_record_id = '61444871' AND NOT d.is_sample AND r.source_snapshot_hash = '97c4a95e70c26ee0b2d43bca70323205d3a0ea14fa1c0c68b3cf820558a24a3c' AND r.preprocessing_version = 'ingest-1'),  E'{"author": "Daragh Thomas", "content": "<p><strong>CrowdStrike Holdings Inc.</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CRWD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"CRWD\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CRWD\\">CRWD</a>)</a> reports fiscal second-quarter results after Wednesday&#8217;s closing bell.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Polymarket traders put the <a href=\\"https://polymarket.com/event/crwd-quarterly-earnings-nongaap-eps-08-26-2026-0pt29/crwd-quarterly-earnings-nongaap-eps-08-26-2026-0pt29\\">odds</a> of adjusted earnings topping 29 cents per share at 80%. The livelier action is on <a href=\\"https://kalshi.com/markets/kxearningsmentioncrwd/crowdstrike-earnings/kxearningsmentioncrwd-26aug26\\">Kalshi</a>, where traders are betting on which words CEO <strong>George Kurtz</strong> and his team will say.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>CrowdStrike guided revenue to about $1.44 billion, but investors may care more about net new ARR. The company expects $284 million to $286 million, up from $256 million last quarter, offering a clearer test of whether Kurtz&#8217;s AI security pitch is translating into new business.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">What Kalshi Predicts CrowdStrike Will Say</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Falcon Flex&#8221; leads the board at 98%. Flex, CrowdStrike&#8217;s flexible subscription model, passed $1.9 billion in ending ARR last quarter, up more than 99% year over year. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Consolidation,&#8221; at 86%, is the thesis behind Flex: replacing multiple security vendors with one Falcon platform.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Mythos&#8221; trades at 85%. Kurtz called Anthropic&#8217;s Mythos release an &#8220;inflection point&#8221; last quarter, arguing that more capable AI can both find and weaponize vulnerabilities. CrowdStrike has since built Project QuiltWorks around defending against that threat.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Nvidia&#8221; trades at 80%. CrowdStrike has embedded Falcon protection into <strong>Nvidia Corp.</strong>&#8216;s <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"NVDA\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\">NVDA</a>)</a> AI-agent infrastructure and hired former Nvidia engineering leader Bartley Richardson as its AI chief.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;AWS&#8221; trades at 77%. CrowdStrike teamed with Amazon this month on an AI-agent red-teaming challenge focused on threats such as prompt injection and agent hijacking.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;OpenAI&#8221; sits at 74%. CrowdStrike is a launch partner in OpenAI&#8217;s Trusted Access for Cyber program, while both companies are also prominent sponsors of next week&#8217;s Fal.Con.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Acquisition&#8221; trades at 72%. CrowdStrike has been an active buyer, most recently agreeing to acquire XM Cyber&#8217;s intellectual property from Schwarz Digits. &#8220;XM Cyber&#8221; itself trades at 63%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Cerebras&#8221; sits at 61%. CrowdStrike partnered with <strong>Cerebras</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CBRS\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CBRS\\">CBRS</a>)</a> in July to speed up Falcon&#8217;s AI threat detection, with the idea that AI-powered attacks increasingly require defenses that can respond at machine speed.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">What Kalshi Predicts CrowdStrike Will Skip</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;AI Detection&#8221; and &#8220;Continuous Identity&#8221; both trade at 45%. Falcon AI Detection and Response grew more than 250% sequentially last quarter with a $50 million-plus pipeline, while Continuous Identity controls what autonomous AI agents can access.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;China&#8221; trades at just 22%, even though CrowdStrike research links China-nexus adversaries to more than 58% of state-sponsored targeted intrusions against the technology sector.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>&#8220;Gen AI,&#8221; at 6%, may say the most: CrowdStrike&#8217;s vocabulary has moved on to agents and agentic AI.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Reading the Board</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Kurtz ended last quarter calling accelerating ARR &#8220;the AI tailwind in action.&#8221; Investors will want to see that tailwind in net new ARR, not just hear about it on stage at Fal.Con.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The beat may be the easy part. The bigger question is whether AI is expanding CrowdStrike&#8217;s market fast enough to support Kurtz&#8217;s pitch that cybersecurity is becoming critical AI infrastructure.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Image: Shutterstock</em></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Kalshi and Benzinga have an existing data collaboration agreement.</em></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/08/61432431/nvidia-ai-race-god-bless-america-etf\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nGod Bless America ETF Exec Says Nvidia Wins No Matter Who Leads AI Race: &#039;Pioneers Die With Arrows in Their Backs&#039;</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>", "created_at": "2026-08-26T18:51:55Z", "headline": "Crowdstrike Earnings Prediction Market Preview: What Will George Kurtz Say About AI?", "id": 61444871, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Sunnyvale--California-Us---November-16--.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Sunnyvale--California-Us---November-16--.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Sunnyvale--California-Us---November-16--.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "CrowdStrike reports earnings as traders bet on Falcon Flex, Mythos and Nvidia, while investors watch whether AI is accelerating net new ARR.", "symbols": ["CBRS", "CRWD", "NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-26T18:51:55Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/08/61444871/crowdstrike-earnings-prediction-market-preview"}'::jsonb, '6f36e308d4ce3614cdf679be391e6d3cc72caeb6faa6708ba28035ff2f43b41d', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61444871/97c4a95e70c2.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.374505+00:00'::timestamptz
