These are the top stocks that gained the attention of retail traders and investors through the day:

## NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA)

Nvidia stock fell by 1.59%, closing at $209.66. The stock reached an intraday high of $213.60 and a low of $209.23, with a 52-week range of $164.07 to $236.54. In the after-hours session, the stock rose 4.71% to $219.53.

The Jensen Huang-led company reported second-quarter revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year over year and above the $92.18 billion analyst estimate, while adjusted EPS of $2.22 also beat expectations of $2.10. The company guided for third-quarter revenue of $105.84 billion-$110.16 billion, above Wall Street’s $104.20 billion estimate, though the slower year-over-year growth rate and exclusion of China data center revenue weighed on shares after hours.

