Photo Courtesy: ChrisStock82 on Shutterstock.com', 'CrowdStrike Posts Best Quarter Ever, but Cathie Wood''s Ark Sells Shares Amid Cloudflare, Cerebras Buys

On Wednesday, Aug. 26, 2026, Ark Invest sold CrowdStrike and AMD shares after CrowdStrike''s record quarter.

On Wednesday, Cathie Wood-led Ark Invest made significant trades involving several prominent stocks, including Cloudflare Inc. (NYSE:NET), Cerebras Systems Inc. (NASDAQ:CBRS), Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO), Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD), and CrowdStrike Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:CRWD).

## The Cloudflare Trade

Ark Invest made a notable move with Cloudflare shares. The company recently reported impressive second-quarter earnings, surpassing expectations with earnings of 29 cents per share against an estimated 27 cents. Revenue reached $696.06 million, exceeding the forecast of $665.5 million.

The stock closed at $284.89 on Wednesday. Ark’s purchase of 47,794 Cloudflare shares was executed through ARK Innovation ETF (BATS:ARKK), ARK Next Generation Internet ETF (BATS:ARKW) and ARK Blockchain & Fintech Innovation ETF (BATS:ARKF), with the transaction valued at approximately $13.6 million based on the closing price.

Read Also: Apple''s ''Surprise and Shine'' iPhone 18 Teaser Has This Analyst Seeing a Big Camera Upgrade and New Color

## The Cerebras Trade

Ark Invest also engaged in trading Cerebras Systems. The company recently launched the CS-4, an AI server system aimed at challenging Nvidia with its advanced wafer-scale chips.

On Wednesday, CBRS closed at $182.15. Ark’s purchase of 49,241 CBRS shares was conducted through ARKK and ARKW, with the transaction valued at approximately $9 million based on the closing price.

Notably, on Tuesday, Wood purchased $17.2 million worth of Cerebras stock.

## The Broadcom Trade

Broadcom was another focus for Ark Invest. The company faced scrutiny over its AI expansion financing, with a potential $370 billion debt looming.

Despite this, Ark saw value in buying 57,705 AVGO shares. The stock closed at $355.59, down 0.32%. Ark’s trade in AVGO was executed through ARK Autonomous Technology & Robotics ETF (BATS:ARKQ), ARKK, AKRW, with the transaction valued at approximately $20.5 million based on the closing price.

## The AMD Trade

Raymond James analyst Simon Leopold recently upgraded AMD from Outperform to Strong Buy and raised the price target to $641 from $565, citing growing demand for server CPUs driven by AI workloads. AMD closed at $456.74 on Monday.

Ark’s sale of 37,977 AMD shares was conducted through ARKK, ARKW, ARKQ and ARKF, with the transaction valued at approximately $18.3 million based on the closing price.

On Tuesday, Ark sold $3.6 million worth of AMD stock.

## The CrowdStrike Trade

Ark Invest sold 14,339 CrowdStrike shares. The company reported a strong second quarter on Wednesday, with revenue of $1.47 billion, surpassing estimates. “Q2 was the best quarter in CrowdStrike’s history," said George Kurtz, founder and CEO of CrowdStrike

CRWD’s stock closed at $189.18. Ark’s trade in CRWD was executed through ARKW, with the transaction valued at approximately $2.7 million based on the closing price.

Other Key Trades:

- Sold 15,183 shares of Brera Holdings PLC (SLMT) through ARKK, 6,012 shares from ARKW and 3,805 shares from ARKF.
- Sold 14,965 shares of Roblox Corp (RBLX) through ARKK.
- Sold 25,009 shares of Robinhood Markets Inc. through ARKW.

Benzinga Edge Stock Rankings indicate CrowdStrike stock has a Momentum score in the 95th percentile.

