er guidance above estimates.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>Benzinga&#8217;s Edge Stock Rankings </strong>indicate that SMTC maintains a strong price trend in the long term but a weak trend in the short and medium terms, with a poor growth score.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\\"><a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMTC\\"><img loading=\\"lazy\\" decoding=\\"async\\" width=\\"768\\" height=\\"114\\" src=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044601/SMTC-EDGE-AUG-26.png\\" alt=\\"Benzinga''s Edge Stock Rankings for SMTC.\\" class=\\"wp-image-1618369\\" style=\\"width:920px;height:auto\\" srcset=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044601/SMTC-EDGE-AUG-26.png 768w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044601/SMTC-EDGE-AUG-26-300x45.png 300w\\" sizes=\\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\\" /></a></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Datavault AI</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>Datavault AI Inc.</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"DVLT\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DVLT\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DVLT\\">DVLT</a>)</a> jumped 4.75% after Nasdaq granted it an extension to regain compliance by Feb. 22, 2027.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>Benzinga&#8217;s Edge Stock Rankings</strong> indicate that DVLT maintains a weak price trend in the long, short, and medium terms.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\\"><a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DVLT\\"><img loading=\\"lazy\\" decoding=\\"async\\" width=\\"763\\" height=\\"114\\" src=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044326/DVLT-EDGE-AUG-26.png\\" alt=\\"Benzinga''s Edge Stock Rankings for DVLT.\\" class=\\"wp-image-1618359\\" style=\\"width:920px;height:auto\\" srcset=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044326/DVLT-EDGE-AUG-26.png 763w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044326/DVLT-EDGE-AUG-26-300x45.png 300w\\" sizes=\\"(max-width: 763px) 100vw, 763px\\" /></a></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Nvidia</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>NVIDIA Corp. </strong><a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"NVDA\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\">NVDA</a>)</a> was 0.30% higher as Wall Street expects it to post quarterly earnings of $2.09 per share on revenue of $92.01 billion after the closing bell.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li><strong>Benzinga&#8217;s Edge Stock Rankings</strong> indicate that NVDA maintains a strong price trend in the short, long, and medium terms, with a solid quality score.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\\"><a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\"><img loading=\\"lazy\\" decoding=\\"async\\" width=\\"760\\" height=\\"112\\" src=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044317/NVDA-EDGE-AUG-26-1.png\\" alt=\\"Benzinga''s Edge Stock Rankings for NVDA.\\" class=\\"wp-image-1618358\\" style=\\"width:920px;height:auto\\" srcset=\\"https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044317/NVDA-EDGE-AUG-26-1.png 760w, https://editorial-assets.benzinga.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/26044317/NVDA-EDGE-AUG-26-1-300x44.png 300w\\" sizes=\\"(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\\" /></a></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/08/61425878/stock-market-will-sp-500-open-up-or-down-today-24\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nStock Market: Will S&amp;P 500 Open Up or Down Today?</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Cues From Last Session</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Information technology, communication services, and materials stocks led the gains on Tuesday, while energy and consumer staples closed lower, as U.S. stocks settled higher with the Dow Jones gaining over 150 points for its third straight win amid falling Treasury yields.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Index</strong></td><td><strong>Performance (+/-)</strong></td><td><strong>Value</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Dow Jones</td><td>0.30%</td><td>53,577.40</td></tr><tr><td>S&amp;P 500</td><td>0.32%</td><td>7,677.28</td></tr><tr><td>Nasdaq Composite</td><td>0.66%</td><td>26,151.30</td></tr><tr><td>Russell 2000</td><td>0.50%</td><td>3,010.02</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Insights From Analysts</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>LPL Financial</strong> expects strong corporate earnings growth to continue providing a solid foundation for the U.S. stock market. In their Weekly Market Commentary, <strong>Jeff Buchbinder</strong>, Chief Equity Strategist for LPL Financial, noted that an improving earnings outlook helps offset potential headwinds like interest rate volatility and geopolitical risks.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61426644/warren-buffett-style-cash-flow-stocks-could-face-heavy-downside-in-openai-era-warns-dwarkesh-patel\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nWarren Buffett-Style Cash Flow Stocks Could Face Heavy Downside in OpenAI Era, Warns Dwarkesh Patel</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p>Highlighting this strong fundamental backdrop, he stated: &#8220;Improving and broadening earnings growth is likely to raise the floor for stocks, and the S&amp;P 500&#8217;s recent technical breakout to new highs probably raises the ceiling.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>While the technology sector and artificial intelligence remain primary growth catalysts, LPL Financial emphasizes that earnings strength has widened across the broader market. From a macroeconomic perspective, LPL expects &#8220;resilient economic growth&#8221; alongside lower oil prices and ebbing inflation over time.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>They project the 10-year Treasury yield will edge lower to the 4% to 4.5% range by year-end, which should help prevent interest rates from creating a larger headwind for equities.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Overall, LPL Financial maintains an optimistic stance on stocks, concluding that &#8220;a supportive fundamental backdrop raises the floor&#8221; for market performance through the remainder of the year.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Upcoming Economic Data</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Here’s what investors will be keeping an eye on Wednesday.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li>July&#8217;s durable goods orders, second estimate second-quarter GDP, July&#8217;s personal income, consumer spending, PCE price index, and core PCE price index data will all be released by 8:30 a.m. ET.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>​Q2 GDP (Second Estimate): Confirmed real gross domestic product grew at an annual rate of 1.5%, slowing from Q1&#8217;s 2.1% pace.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>​July PCE Data: Headline PCE price index rose 0.2% MoM (3.7% YoY), while core PCE (excluding food and energy) rose 0.2% MoM (3.3% YoY).</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\"><strong>Commodities, Crypto, And Global Equity Markets</strong></h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Crude Oil WTI futures were trading lower in the early New York session by 2.61% to hover around $80.21 per barrel.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Gold Spot US Dollar fell 0.72% to hover around $4,625.39 per ounce. The U.S. Dollar Index spot was 0.01% higher at the 98.9230 level.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Meanwhile, <strong>Bitcoin </strong><a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"BTC\\" data-exchange=\\"CRYPTO\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BTC-USD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(CRYPTO: BTC)</a> was trading 1.50% higher at $78,979.57 per coin over the last 24 hours.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Asian markets were mixed on Wednesday, as Australia’s ASX 200, South Korea’s Kospi, and India&#8217;s Nifty 50 indices fell. Hong Kong’s Hang Seng, China&#8217;s CSI 300 and Japan’s Nikkei 225 indices rose. European markets were also mixed in early trading.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/earnings/26/08/61426144/shay-boloor-highlights-nvidias-fundamentally-illogical-valuation-discount-as-nvda-eyes-world-leader-status-in-cpus\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nShay Boloor Highlights Nvidia&#039;s &#039;Fundamentally Illogical&#039; Valuation Discount As NVDA Eyes &#039;World Leader&#039; Status In CPUs</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Photo courtesy: Shutterstock</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-26T09:30:12Z", "headline": "Stock Market Today: Dow Jones Futures Rise, S&P 500 Slips Ahead of NVDA Q2 as Core PCE Comes in at 3.3% — Zoom, Intuit, Datavault AI in Focus (UPDATED)", "id": 61427410, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Wall-Street.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Wall-Street.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/Wall-Street.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "U.S. stock futures were mixed on Wednesday, as the Dow Jones index rose, while the S&amp;P 500 and Nasdaq 100 indices slipped.", "symbols": ["BTCUSD", "DVLT", "INTU", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SMTC", "SPY", "ZM"], "updated_at": "2026-08-26T13:02:46Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/08/61427410/stock-market-today-dow-jones-futures-rise-sp-500-slips-ahead-of-nvda-q2-earnings-and-feds-preferred-inflation-data-zoom-intuit-datavault-ai-in-focus"}'::jsonb, 'f789cb1295eb9ebba24fee9bd82b287a920c1932343b78742d1d76841c6055b4', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61427410/170fa2905cc5.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.248268+00:00'::timestamptz
