SELECT (SELECT r.revision_id FROM document_revision r JOIN document d ON d.document_id = r.document_id WHERE d.provider_id = (SELECT provider_id FROM provider WHERE code = 'alpaca') AND d.source_namespace = 'news' AND d.source_record_id = '61477237' AND NOT d.is_sample AND r.source_snapshot_hash = '8dcc8e3934e45890d57773b52a99974b5c5f75ee64072a2e56dcf77e89a30983' AND r.preprocessing_version = 'ingest-1'),  E'{"author": "Daragh Thomas", "content": "<p><strong>Masayoshi Son</strong> is circling another multibillion-dollar AI bet as <strong>SoftBank Group Corp.</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SFTBY\\">(OTC:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SFTBY\\">SFTBY</a>)</a> is reportedly in talks to buy a majority stake in <strong>1X Technologies</strong>, the OpenAI-backed humanoid robot maker, at a valuation of roughly $6 billion.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The negotiations, first reported by The Information, remain ongoing and could still fall apart. SoftBank declined to comment.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The eye-catching part is what Son may be valuing at $6 billion: a company whose flagship NEO robot has yet to reach a customer, but which is already taking paid reservations while <strong>Tesla Inc.</strong> <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TSLA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"TSLA\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TSLA\\">TSLA</a>)</a>  works toward a consumer Optimus launch.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Traders on <a href=\\"https://polymarket.com/event/will-tesla-release-optimus-by-june-30-2026\\">Polymarket</a>, meanwhile, give Tesla just a 3% chance of making Optimus available for purchase or paid preorder by the end of 2026.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">From $375 Million to $6 Billion</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>1X&#8217;s valuation has exploded in just three years.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>When SoftBank first discussed backing the company in 2023, 1X was seeking funding at a $375 million pre-money valuation. By January 2025, a financing valued it at roughly $820 million.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Later that year, 1X went looking for as much as $1 billion at a $10 billion valuation, though it ultimately raised less than half of what it sought.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Now SoftBank is reportedly circling again, this time at <a href=\\"https://www.theinformation.com/articles/softbank-talks-buy-majority-stake-humanoid-maker-1x-6-billion-valuation\\">roughly</a> $6 billion.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>That would still value 1X at more than seven times its early-2025 price.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">What SoftBank Would Be Buying</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>NEO is a humanoid designed mainly for household chores, priced at $20,000 outright or $499 per month.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>1X says it booked its entire first-year production capacity of 10,000 units within five days. U.S. deliveries are due to begin in 2026 from its new California manufacturing base.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Early units won&#8217;t be fully autonomous, however. 1X says harder tasks may still require remote assistance from one of its human &#8220;Experts.&#8221;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">The OpenAI Connection Runs Deep</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>OpenAI&#8217;s Startup Fund led a $23.5 million funding round for 1X in 2023, and OpenAI itself reportedly explored acquiring the company outright in 2025 before those talks collapsed.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Now SoftBank, one of OpenAI&#8217;s largest financial backers, may take control instead. Its cumulative investment in OpenAI is expected to reach $64.6 billion, representing roughly a 13% stake.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">1X Gets a Head Start on Tesla</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Elon Musk has said consumer Optimus sales could begin by the end of 2027, but Tesla&#8217;s timetable has already slipped more than once.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Polymarket traders see little chance of a consumer launch this year. 1X, by contrast, is already taking paid reservations for NEO, even though customer deliveries have yet to begin.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Tesla is planning on a vastly larger scale. Its first Optimus production line is designed for eventual capacity of 1 million robots a year. 1X says its current facilities can produce up to 10,000 NEOs annually, with plans to surpass 100,000 by the end of 2027.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>For now, 1X may be tiny next to Tesla, but it has beaten Musk to one important milestone: the order button.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Image: Shutterstock</em></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/08/61464185/kevin-warsh-jackson-hole-prediction-markets\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nJackson Hole Prediction Market Preview: What Will Kevin Warsh Say?</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>", "created_at": "2026-08-27T18:46:13Z", "headline": "Tesla''s Optimus Rival Could Be Worth $6 Billion As SoftBank Circles OpenAI-Backed 1X", "id": 61477237, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Scottsdale--Arizona---Aug--08-2023-A-New.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Scottsdale--Arizona---Aug--08-2023-A-New.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Scottsdale--Arizona---Aug--08-2023-A-New.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "SoftBank may value OpenAI-backed 1X at $6 billion as NEO takes preorders and traders give Tesla just 3% odds of a 2026 Optimus preorder.", "symbols": ["NVDA", "SFTBY", "TSLA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-27T18:46:13Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/08/61477237/softbank-1x-6-billion-tesla-optimus"}'::jsonb, '0c4d201bf96ae8632f2e18166bc1b9ab09c277ca70405c2a3faa9f00564a7c5c', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61477237/8dcc8e3934e4.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.915013+00:00'::timestamptz
