trong></th>\\n<th><strong>Gross Profit (in billions)</strong></th>\\n<th><strong>Revenue Growth</strong></th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>NVIDIA Corp</td>\\n<td>32.63</td>\\n<td>26.40</td>\\n<td>20.56</td>\\n<td>33.06%</td>\\n<td>$71.0</td>\\n<td>$61.16</td>\\n<td>85.23%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Broadcom Inc</td>\\n<td>59.36</td>\\n<td>19.35</td>\\n<td>23.06</td>\\n<td>11.11%</td>\\n<td>$13.07</td>\\n<td>$15.41</td>\\n<td>47.87%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Micron Technology Inc</td>\\n<td>21.09</td>\\n<td>10.46</td>\\n<td>11.77</td>\\n<td>32.62%</td>\\n<td>$35.58</td>\\n<td>$35.06</td>\\n<td>345.72%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Advanced Micro Devices Inc</td>\\n<td>122.24</td>\\n<td>11.64</td>\\n<td>19.14</td>\\n<td>3.49%</td>\\n<td>$3.35</td>\\n<td>$6.2</td>\\n<td>50.11%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Texas Instruments Inc</td>\\n<td>39.52</td>\\n<td>13.19</td>\\n<td>12.23</td>\\n<td>11.32%</td>\\n<td>$2.95</td>\\n<td>$3.35</td>\\n<td>22.82%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Marvell Technology Inc</td>\\n<td>82.60</td>\\n<td>11.86</td>\\n<td>24.10</td>\\n<td>0.21%</td>\\n<td>$0.66</td>\\n<td>$1.26</td>\\n<td>27.57%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Analog Devices Inc</td>\\n<td>44.38</td>\\n<td>5.40</td>\\n<td>13.22</td>\\n<td>3.98%</td>\\n<td>$2.13</td>\\n<td>$2.71</td>\\n<td>39.63%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Qualcomm Inc</td>\\n<td>18.35</td>\\n<td>6.20</td>\\n<td>3.92</td>\\n<td>7.29%</td>\\n<td>$3.04</td>\\n<td>$5.28</td>\\n<td>-4.03%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Monolithic Power Systems Inc</td>\\n<td>79.57</td>\\n<td>16.45</td>\\n<td>19.49</td>\\n<td>6.8%</td>\\n<td>$0.32</td>\\n<td>$0.54</td>\\n<td>47.56%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>NXP Semiconductors NV</td>\\n<td>19.18</td>\\n<td>4.97</td>\\n<td>4.33</td>\\n<td>6.87%</td>\\n<td>$1.27</td>\\n<td>$2.0</td>\\n<td>19.48%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Credo Technology Group Holding Ltd</td>\\n<td>90.24</td>\\n<td>20.47</td>\\n<td>31.93</td>\\n<td>8.64%</td>\\n<td>$0.17</td>\\n<td>$0.3</td>\\n<td>157.02%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Microchip Technology Inc</td>\\n<td>108.09</td>\\n<td>6.19</td>\\n<td>7.86</td>\\n<td>3.14%</td>\\n<td>$0.49</td>\\n<td>$0.94</td>\\n<td>38.05%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>ON Semiconductor Corp</td>\\n<td>47.39</td>\\n<td>3.91</td>\\n<td>4.72</td>\\n<td>3.12%</td>\\n<td>$0.43</td>\\n<td>$0.62</td>\\n<td>9.18%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>GLOBALFOUNDRIES Inc</td>\\n<td>35.88</td>\\n<td>2.13</td>\\n<td>3.70</td>\\n<td>1.41%</td>\\n<td>$0.48</td>\\n<td>$0.51</td>\\n<td>5.81%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Tower Semiconductor Ltd</td>\\n<td>84.13</td>\\n<td>7.80</td>\\n<td>14.21</td>\\n<td>2.99%</td>\\n<td>$0.17</td>\\n<td>$0.14</td>\\n<td>23.66%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>First Solar Inc</td>\\n<td>12.75</td>\\n<td>2.15</td>\\n<td>4.14</td>\\n<td>4.18%</td>\\n<td>$0.61</td>\\n<td>$0.61</td>\\n<td>-3.73%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings Inc</td>\\n<td>84.80</td>\\n<td>13.20</td>\\n<td>17.57</td>\\n<td>6.81%</td>\\n<td>$0.14</td>\\n<td>$0.2</td>\\n<td>35.77%</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><strong>Average</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>59.35</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>9.71</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>13.46</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>7.12%</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>$4.05</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>$4.7</strong></td>\\n<td><strong>53.91%</strong></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\\n\\n<style>\\n        table {\\n            width: 100%;\\n            border-collapse: collapse;\\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\n            font-size: 14px;\\n        }\\n\\n        th, td {\\n            padding: 8px;\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        th {\\n            background-color: #293a5a;\\n            color: #fff;\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        tr:nth-child(even) {\\n            background-color: #f2f4f8;\\n        }\\n\\n        tr:hover {\\n            background-color: #e1e4ea;\\n        }\\n\\n        td:nth-child(3), td:nth-child(5) {\\n            text-align: left;\\n        }\\n\\n        .dividend-amount {\\n            font-weight: bold;\\n            color: #0d6efd;\\n        }\\n\\n        .dividend-frequency {\\n            font-size: 12px;\\n            color: #6c757d;\\n        }\\n    </style>\\n\\n<p>By conducting a comprehensive analysis of NVIDIA, the following trends become evident: </p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<p>The stock''s Price to Earnings ratio of <b>32.63</b> is lower than the industry average by <b>0.55x</b>, suggesting potential value in the eyes of market participants.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>It could be trading at a premium in relation to its book value, as indicated by its Price to Book ratio of <b>26.4</b> which exceeds the industry average by <b>2.72x</b>.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>With a relatively high Price to Sales ratio of <b>20.56</b>, which is <b>1.53x</b> the industry average, the stock might be considered overvalued based on sales performance.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>With a Return on Equity (ROE) of <b>33.06%</b> that is <b>25.94%</b> above the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits efficient use of equity to generate profits.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of <b>$71.0 Billion</b> is <b>17.53x</b> above the industry average, highlighting stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The gross profit of <b>$61.16 Billion</b> is <b>13.01x</b> above that of its industry, highlighting stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>The company''s revenue growth of <b>85.23%</b> exceeds the industry average of <b>53.91%</b>, indicating strong sales performance and market outperformance.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Debt To Equity Ratio</h3>\\n<p><img src=\\"https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/26/d84c1bb348593a32867e944f75874142.png\\" alt=\\"debt to equity\\" /></p>\\n\\n<p>The debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio measures the financial leverage of a company by evaluating its debt relative to its equity.</p>\\n<p>Considering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.</p>\\n<p>When comparing NVIDIA with its top 4 peers based on the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following insights can be observed:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<p>NVIDIA is in a relatively stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers, as evidenced by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of <b>0.06</b>.</p>\\n</li>\\n<li>\\n<p>This implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity.</p>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Key Takeaways</h3>\\n<p>For NVIDIA in the Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment industry, the PE, PB, and PS ratios indicate that the stock is relatively undervalued compared to its peers. However, the high ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth suggest that NVIDIA is performing exceptionally well in terms of profitability and operational efficiency within the industry sector.</p>\\n<p><em>This article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.</em></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-26T09:58:21Z", "headline": "Competitor Analysis: Evaluating NVIDIA And Competitors In Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment Industry", "id": 61427637, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_5.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_5.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2025/11/06/earnings_preview_5.jpg?width=250&height=187"}], "source": "benzinga", "summary": "Amidst the fast-paced and highly competitive business environment of today, conducting comprehensive company analysis is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts. In this article, we will delve into an extensive", "symbols": ["NVDA"], "updated_at": "2026-08-26T09:58:21Z", "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/08/61427637/competitor-analysis-evaluating-nvidia-and-competitors-semiconductors-amp-semiconductor-equipment-ind"}'::jsonb, 'f2d49bc6cce5e452920cd3f61b8398554cd3c008f137b4a5b74def66452a1a82', NULL, NULL, NULL, '["file:/Users/zuttome/LocalDocs/Learning/College/NUS/MTech-AIS/IRS/GC1/always-ignore/architecture-book/evaluation/data/alpaca_windows/0001045810-26-000073.json", "raw/alpaca/articles/61427637/ef5b29d8a77e.json"]'::jsonb, '2026-10-19T04:46:36.255424+00:00'::timestamptz
