INSERT INTO document_revision_source (revision_id, raw_payload, raw_payload_sha256, raw_document, raw_document_sha256, raw_document_url, raw_file_refs, stored_at)
SELECT (SELECT r.revision_id FROM document_revision r JOIN document d ON d.document_id = r.document_id WHERE d.provider_id = (SELECT provider_id FROM provider WHERE code = 'alpaca') AND d.source_namespace = 'news' AND d.source_record_id = '61474382' AND NOT d.is_sample AND r.source_snapshot_hash = 'f641ec65fd67d25419e3525d1c9bedf28f3c207f887b01fbee3f822996669571' AND r.preprocessing_version = 'ingest-1'),  E'{"author": "Piero Cingari", "content": "<p><strong>Nvidia Corp.</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"NVDA\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA\\">NVDA</a>)</a>&#8216;s forecast for a roughly 70% revenue surge next fiscal year sent the chipmaker up 9% Thursday, eyeing its best-performing <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/large-cap/26/08/61468560/nvidia-stock-adds-370-billion-market-value\\">day since April 2025. </a></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>A staggering rally in cybersecurity stocks, fueled by optimism over agentic AI demand, has triggered an unusual shift beneath the surface. Technology was the only S&amp;P 500 sector in the green by midday, with the other 10 all lower. In addition:</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li>The S&amp;P 500 rose 0.8% to 7,734.44, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average added 0.4% to 53,663.52, advancing 200 points.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The Nasdaq 100 rallied almost 1% to about 29,500 points.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>Bond yields stabilized ahead of Kevin Warsh&#8217;s highly anticipated speech at Jackson Hole on Friday.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The 10-year Treasury yield held at 4.66%, while the 30-year yield was at 5.18%. </li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Thursday&#8217;s Data Hands Hawks Ammunition</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Initial jobless claims fell 4,000 to 203,000 against forecasts for 208,000, wholesale inventories jumped 1.3% versus the 0.2% consensus, and the Kansas City Fed manufacturing production index held at 17, its highest since April 2022.&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Crude firmed modestly. West Texas Intermediate rose 0.6% to $82.73 a barrel, while Brent added 1.2% to $88.85, both still nursing weekly losses of roughly 5% on signs of diplomatic progress in the Middle East.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Gold edged up 0.3% to $4,606.62 an ounce, with the&nbsp;<strong>SPDR Gold Shares&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GLD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/GLD\\">GLD</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;tracking the move. Silver was the stronger metal, rising 1.8% to $69.35 an ounce. <strong>Bitcoin</strong> <a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"BTC\\" data-exchange=\\"CRYPTO\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BTC-USD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(CRYPTO: BTC)</a> rallied 2.7% above $80,000. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Thursday&#8217;s Performance In Major US Indices</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><thead><tr><th>Index</th><th>Last</th><th>% Change</th><th>MTD</th><th>YTD</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>S&amp;P 500</td><td>7,734.44</td><td>+0.8%</td><td>+3.3%</td><td>+13.1%</td></tr><tr><td>Dow Jones</td><td>53,663.52</td><td>+0.4%</td><td>+2.3%</td><td>+11.6%</td></tr><tr><td>Nasdaq 100</td><td>29,484</td><td>+0.9%</td><td>+4.7%</td><td>+17.2%</td></tr><tr><td>Russell 2000</td><td>3,016.29</td><td>+0.4%</td><td>+3.0%</td><td>+21.9%</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\\"wp-element-caption\\"><em>Updated by 1:00 PM ET</em></figcaption></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>According to the&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://bzresearch.myclickfunnels.com/benzinga-pro-content-webinar-registration/?utm_source=BZprocontent082726&amp;t=be2bearmibe3na1\\">Benzinga Pro</a>&nbsp;platform:</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<ul class=\\"wp-block-list\\">\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>Vanguard S&amp;P 500 ETF&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/VOO\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/VOO\\">VOO</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;gained 0.7%.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DIA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DIA\\">DIA</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;rose 0.4%.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>Invesco QQQ Trust&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/QQQ\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/QQQ\\">QQQ</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;climbed 0.9%.</li>\\n\\n\\n\\n<li>The&nbsp;<strong>iShares Russell 2000 ETF&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IWM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IWM\\">IWM</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;advanced 0.4%.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Cybersecurity Melts Up While The Other Ten Sectors Bleed</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLK\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLK\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLK\\">XLK</a>)</a> surged 2.9% and was the only one of the 11 S&amp;P 500 sector funds to advance. The&nbsp;<strong>Consumer Staples Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLP\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLP\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLP\\">XLP</a>)</a> was the worst performer, down 1.0%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Losses elsewhere were tightly clustered. The&nbsp;<strong>Communication Services Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLC\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLC\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLC\\">XLC</a>)</a> fell 0.8%, the&nbsp;<strong>Utilities Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLU\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLU\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLU\\">XLU</a>)</a> slid 0.7% and the&nbsp;<strong>Energy Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLE\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLE\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLE\\">XLE</a>)</a> dropped 0.6% despite firmer crude. The&nbsp;<strong>Financial Select Sector SPDR Fund</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLF\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"XLF\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/XLF\\">XLF</a>)</a> was the most resilient decliner at 0.4%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>Industry-level dispersion was extreme. The&nbsp;<strong>iShares Expanded Tech-Software Sector ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IGV\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"IGV\\" data-exchange=\\"BATS\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(BATS:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/IGV\\">IGV</a>)</a> rocketed 6.9%, easily the standout, while the&nbsp;<strong>VanEck Semiconductor ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMH\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"SMH\\" data-exchange=\\"NASDAQ\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SMH\\">SMH</a>)</a> added 2.9% and the&nbsp;<strong>Invesco Solar ETF</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TAN\\" target=\\"_blank\\" class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"TAN\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/TAN\\">TAN</a>)</a> rose 1.9%.&nbsp;</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The <strong>Global X Cybersecurity ETF </strong><a class=\\"ticker-link\\" data-ticker=\\"BUG\\" data-exchange=\\"ARCA\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BUG\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BUG\\">BUG</a>)</a> was up 9.7%. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Thursday&#8217;s Stock Movers</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Okta Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/OKTA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/OKTA\\">OKTA</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;was the best performer in the Russell 1000, soaring 28.0% to $172.10 after fiscal second-quarter adjusted earnings of $1.05 per share beat the $0.97 consensus on revenue of $805 million versus $795 million expected. The identity provider raised full-year adjusted EPS guidance to $3.90-$3.94 against a $3.84 Street estimate and said AI-focused products such as Okta for AI Agents accounted for roughly 30% of new bookings.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Salesforce Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CRM\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CRM\\">CRM</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;jumped 21.0% to $248.77 after posting second-quarter adjusted EPS of $5.90 on revenue of $11.35 billion, up 10.8% year-on-year, and lifting its fiscal 2027 revenue outlook by $300 million in constant currency to $46.1 billion-$46.4 billion. Results included a $2.6 billion gain on its stake in Anthropic, alongside the launch of Claudeforce.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>CrowdStrike Holdings Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CRWD\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CRWD\\">CRWD</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;rallied 17.6% to $222.38 on record net new annual recurring revenue of $333 million, up 51% year-on-year, and adjusted EPS of $0.31 that extended its beat streak to nine quarters. Management raised fiscal 2027 net new ARR growth guidance by 630 basis points to 34% at the midpoint.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Veeva Systems Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/VEEV\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/VEEV\\">VEEV</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;climbed 17.1% to $286.87 after reporting quarterly EPS of $2.35 against a $2.22 consensus on revenue of $928 million, up 17.6%, and raising fiscal 2027 EPS guidance to $9.21 and revenue guidance to $3.682 billion-$3.687 billion.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Figma Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FIG\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FIG\\">FIG</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;rounded out the top five, up 14.3% to $30.88. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div class=\\"bz-read-next-block\\"\\n     data-variant=\\"card\\"\\n     data-news-mode=\\"manual\\"\\n\\n    >\\n\\n\\n<p>\\n<strong>\\nRead Also:\\n<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/08/61472513/crowdstrike-stock-best-day-ever-analyst-price-targets\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">\\nCrowdStrike Stock&#039;s Best Day Ever: These 11 Analysts Raised Targets</a>\\n</strong>\\n</p>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Cybersecurity Complex Went Vertical Behind CrowdStrike, Okta</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Palo Alto Networks Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/PANW\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/PANW\\">PANW</a>)</a></strong> rose 12.1% ahead of its Sept. 1 results, <strong>Zscaler Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ZS\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/ZS\\">ZS</a>)</a></strong> gained 10.5%, <strong>SentinelOne Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/S\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/S\\">S</a>)</a></strong> added 9.8%, <strong>Fortinet Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FTNT\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FTNT\\">FTNT</a>)</a></strong> rose 7.2%, and <strong>SailPoint Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SAIL\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/SAIL\\">SAIL</a>)</a></strong> advanced 13.8% despite not reporting until Sept. 9.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p>The pain was concentrated in staples, retail and hardware. <strong>Hormel Foods Corp. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/HRL\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/HRL\\">HRL</a>)</a></strong> was the worst name in the index, tumbling 9.2% to $21.52 after third-quarter adjusted EPS of 37 cents arrived alongside a cut to full-year sales guidance to $12.1 billion-$12.2 billion and a slashed diluted EPS range of $1.06-$1.12 from $1.28-$1.37, with management citing weak retail demand and soft private-label snack nut volumes.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Everpure Inc. <a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/P\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/P\\">P</a>)</a></strong> sank 8.4% to $99.72 despite 38% revenue growth and a sharply raised full-year outlook, as investors focused on negative second-quarter free cash flow and a gross margin running at the low end of the company&#8217;s target range, while it prioritizes share gains over near-term profitability.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Burlington Stores Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BURL\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NYSE:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/BURL\\">BURL</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;fell 6.4% to $293.96 as second-quarter sales landed below analyst estimates even with total sales up 11% and comparable store sales up 2%. The bleed spread across the off-price and discount complex, with&nbsp;<strong>Dollar Tree Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DLTR\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/DLTR\\">DLTR</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;down 4.0% and&nbsp;<strong>Five Below Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FIVE\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/FIVE\\">FIVE</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;off 3.6%.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Moderna Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MRNA\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MRNA\\">MRNA</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;dropped 5.7% to $141.20 after announcing a $2.0 billion private placement of convertible senior notes due 2032. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><strong>Celsius Holdings Inc.&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CELH\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noreferrer noopener\\">(NASDAQ:<a class=\\"ticker\\" href=\\"https://www.benzinga.com/quote/CELH\\">CELH</a>)</a></strong>&nbsp;slid 5.0% to $33.48 after Deutsche Bank downgraded the energy drink maker to Hold from Buy. </p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Thursday&#8217;s Russell 1000 Top Gainers</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>% change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Okta, Inc.</strong></td><td>+28.03%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Salesforce, Inc.</strong></td><td>+20.99%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.</strong></td><td>+17.55%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Veeva Systems Inc.</strong></td><td>+17.13%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Figma, Inc.</strong></td><td>+14.25%</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<h2 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Thursday&#8217;s Russell 1000 Top Losers</h2>\\n\\n\\n\\n<figure class=\\"wp-block-table is-style-stripes\\"><table class=\\"has-fixed-layout\\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>% change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Hormel Foods Corporation</strong></td><td>-9.22%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Everpure, Inc.</strong></td><td>-8.43%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Burlington Stores, Inc.</strong></td><td>-6.38%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Moderna, Inc.</strong></td><td>-5.65%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Celsius Holdings, Inc.</strong></td><td>-4.96%</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><em>Image: Shutterstock</em><br></p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<p><br></p>", "created_at": "2026-08-27T17:25:23Z", "headline": "Nvidia''s Best Day Since April 2025, Cybersecurity Stocks Go Vertical: Stock Market Today", "id": 61474382, "images": [{"size": "large", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Global-Stock-Market-Rally-And-Bullish-Pe.jpg?width=2048&height=1536"}, {"size": "small", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Global-Stock-Market-Rally-And-Bullish-Pe.jpg?width=1024&height=768"}, {"size": "thumb", "url": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/08/27/Global-Stock-Market-Rally-And-Bullish-Pe.